SUMMARY:Understanding the DULF Verdict - by Canadian Drug Policy Coalition
LOCATION:Virtual
DESCRIPTION:More info:
  https://us06web.zoom.us/webinar/register/1317907275222/WN_g4KZbMPbR6-rOU-
 ini8_rQ?fbclid=PAdGRleAUqxMxleHRuA2FlbQIxMQBwZG9mAmZkaWQWUPfQ_0Urew6TDiVLu
 W3TSPeJFVfnI3NydGMGYXBwX2lkDzEyNDAyNDU3NDI4NzQxNAABp6YQ0bm_m-GU7e4iB0DwwJc
 YTg-C3MC-8Wxg-cJwyHSqP33KHF5iH0I9DP4J_aem_kSJU0w5VJwzDesICvGAsfw#/registra
 tion\n\nHosted by Canadian Drug Policy Coalition
  (https://www.drugpolicy.ca/)\n\nOn September 29 the BC Supreme Court
  ruled that the criminal law used to arrest and convict DULF co-founders
  Jeremy Kalicum and Eris Nyx is unconstitutional. Join a panel of experts
  for a Q&A on the judgement\, legal arguments\, and what this decision
  might hold for the future of drug policy in Canada.\n
END:VEVENT
