SUMMARY: Killer B Cinema Presents: Srigala!
DESCRIPTION:On Friday\, October 2nd\, join us for the Indonesian Friday t
 he 13th! Where summer camp is still dangerous!\n\nAdvanced tickets are $5
  (plus Eventbrite service fee)\; tickets at the door are $8 (Space is lim
 ited\, and tickets sell out fast)!\n\nDoors open at 7:30 pm\, and the mov
 ie begins at 8:00.\n\nTicket link: https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/killer-b-c
 inema-presents-srigala-tickets-1999863321028?aff=oddtdtcreator https://ww
 w.eventbrite.ca/e/killer-b-cinema-presents-srigala-tickets-1999863321028?
 aff=oddtdtcreator\n\n*NO outside food or drinks\; please buy food and dri
 nks from the venue.\n\n*All films have closed captioning.\n\nMovie info:\
 n\nIt’s the month of Halloween\, and what better time to see the Friday t
 he 13th rip-off you’ve probably never seen!\n\nSrigala is Indonesia’s won
 derfully wild take on the original Friday the 13th. And if you’re wonderi
 ng\, “Is this a true slasher film?” Absolutely… but with a healthy pinch 
 of Southeast Asian over-the-top cinema thrown into the mix!\n\nConsidered
  an obscure gem of Southeast Asian horror\, Srigala is a must-see\, espec
 ially if you love slashers\, cult horror\, and movies that aren’t afraid 
 to get a little weird.\n\nSrigala was directed by legendary Indonesian fi
 lmmaker Sisworo Gautama Putra\, who also directed the original Satan’s Sl
 aves!\n\nLike Friday the 13th\, the story follows a gaggle of young adult
 s — aka future slasher victims — who make their way to a remote lakeside 
 camp. There’s a little relaxation\, a little fun…and then the chaos begin
 s!\n\nInfo about See-Scape:\n\nOur movies will be shown on the second flo
 or! There are two bars available in See-Scape. The bar on the second floo
 r is open during our event and is cash-only. Debit/Credit purchases are a
 vailable on the main floor.\n\nSee-Scape also has an amazing menu. To lea
 rn more about See-Scape\, please click here! www.seescapeto.com/ https://
 www.seescapeto.com/\n\nSee-Scape is located at 347 Keele Street (the clos
 est intersection is Keele/Dundas) and is easily accessible via TTC. (from
  Keele Station or Dundas West Station)\n\nParking: There is a Green P par
 king lot beside See-Scape and a few other paid parking lots nearby.\n\nEa
 ch month\, join Lizzie Violet & Zoltan Du Lac for killer B-moves from the
  1930s to the present!\n\nPlease like our Facebook page and Instagram @ki
 llerbcinema so you don’t miss an invite.\n\nThank you to See-Scape and th
 eir staff! They make our monthly event extra unforgettable!\n\nWe hope to
  see you at See-Scape.\n\n
CATEGORIES:Film,See-Scape
X-TKF-FEATURED-IMAGE:https://d3flpus5evl89n.cloudfront.net/6755f3e6a02aaf
 1c2599e757/6aa0dc598f563d8adc0adbb9/scaled_1024.jpg
X-TKF-CUSTOM-PREVIEW:On Friday\, October 2nd\, join us for the Indonesian
  Friday the 13th! Where summer camp is still dangerous! Advanced tickets 
 are $5 (plus Eventbrite service...
LOCATION:See-Scape\,347 Keele St\, Toronto\, ON M6P 2K6\, Canada
CREATED:20260909T041107Z
DTSTAMP:20261003T050509Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260909T041133Z
TRANSP:OPAQUE
