BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Torontobotanicalgarden": "https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/event/essence-of-the-garden-plein-air-art-exhibition-sale/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:torontobotanicalgarden
X-SOURCE:Toronto Botanical Garden
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261003T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261018T235959
DTSTAMP:20261003T010544
CREATED:20250718T195137Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260930T182016Z
UID:10001841-1790985600-1792367999@torontobotanicalgarden.ca
SUMMARY:Essence of the Garden: Plein Air Art Exhibition and Sale 
DESCRIPTION:Celebrating Art\, Nature\, and Community — Essence of the Garden is the 2nd annual plein air art exhibition and sale featuring over 100 original artworks created outdoors at Toronto Botanical Garden and Edwards Gardens. This curated\, site-specific show invites visitors to experience the Garden through the eyes of the artists who paint here—capturing moments of light\, movement\, and the essence of the natural world. \n\n\n\nSaturday\, October 3 through 18\, 2026Open Daily\, 10:30 a.m. to 4:30 p.m.Free Admission  \n\n\n\nThis exhibition coincides with Toronto’s Ravine Days\, an annual city-wide celebration of Toronto’s ravine system. \n\n\n\nPresenting Sponsor: Foresters Financial \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n What You’ll See\n\n\n\n\nOver 100 plein air paintings celebrating the Garden created by 46 talented local artists\n\n\n\nArtworks displayed in public spaces across the Visitor Centre and are available for sale.\n\n\n\nVisit the Garden Shop for unique\, artist-made gifts and mini works\n\n\n\nEngage with the artist(s) who will be hosting workshops and will be onsite throughout the exhibition painting ‘plein air’\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nMeet the Artists\n\n\n\n\n\nFunmilola AdeseunJo BaumannZora BilyOlga Olesya BondarevaCarolyn M.BoydMarsha BrownJune BuickPerry ChowTammy Hoy CutlerStella DaiEric DavidLes DeSouzaNatalie DitchburnPaul DolgovVivian EastBarbara EguchiAnastasia EveClaudia FernandezTerri FlaserDoug GeldartDougal M.HaggartHanna HegerDavid Johns \n\n\n\n\n\nLawrence KavanaghJan KrausWin KuploskyLouisa LauSylvia Le RoyHanifa MamujeeMaria Matic (Amrylismatic)Nola McConnanTheo McLarenFariba MirhosseiniTanya MurdochNoelle OberdingTanya OnieogouTina PapoutsisCarolyne PascoePiera PuglieseJenny ReidMargaret RosemanAlexandra SharmaAdele SteinbergCameron StewartRosemary TannockAdriana Toth \n\n\n\n\n\n\nClick here for Artist bios\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nTake Home a Piece of the Garden\n\n\n\nArtwork will be available for purchase throughout the run of the show—buy your favourite painting and take home a piece of the Garden. Additional items from participating artists will be available at the Garden Shop and/or pop-up boutique\, including miniature art\, prints\, cards\, and magnets. Sales support both the artists and Toronto Botanical Garden’s community programming. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nOur Partners\n\n\n\n\nAlexandra Sharma\n\n\n\nDon Valley Art Group\n\n\n\nToronto Heliconian Club\n\n\n\nToronto Watercolour Society\n\n\n\nWillowdale Group of Artists\n\n\n\nWomen’s Art Association of Canada\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\nThank you to Snaptique for capturing highlights of our Opening Night 2025 with their vintage photo booth. Snaptique has been providing fun photo activations since 2014. They are the best photo booth rental in Kitchener\, Ottawa\, and Calgary.
URL:https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/event/essence-of-the-garden-plein-air-art-exhibition-sale/
CATEGORIES:Events
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Plein-Air-2026-Webs.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Torontobotanicalgarden": "https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/event/toronto-gone-wild-ravines/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:torontobotanicalgarden
X-SOURCE:Toronto Botanical Garden
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261003T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261223T235959
DTSTAMP:20261003T010544
CREATED:20260929T182315Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260929T182424Z
UID:10002042-1790985600-1798070399@torontobotanicalgarden.ca
SUMMARY:Toronto Gone Wild: Ravines
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Gone Wild: Ravines\, an indoor exhibit hosted in partnership with Museum of Toronto\, explores our extensive network of ravines\, creating pockets of wilderness throughout the city. The exhibit explores the plants\, wildlife\, and stories found within our ravines—from wildlife to pollinators and native plants—and the many ways people interact with these urban wild spaces. \n\n\n\nOctober 3 through December 2026 | Open daily\, 10:30 a.m. to 4:30 p.m. | Free admission   
URL:https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/event/toronto-gone-wild-ravines/
CATEGORIES:Ravines
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/TGW-Exhibit-3-of-46.jpg
END:VEVENT
