SUMMARY:AI Fundamentals for Kids with MediaSmarts
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261003T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261003T134500
UID:6a904c8c60ccaf01c02166a2@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In this playful\, hands-on workshop\, children will discover t
 hat AI tools are computer programs built by people—they don't think or f
 eel like we do\, they just look for patterns in the examples they're shown
 . Through fun activities\, participants will figure out a "robot's" secret
  rules\, learn why AI sometimes makes mistakes\, and design their very own
  "Trashbot" that learns to tell trash from treasure.\nThis program is desi
 gned for children ages 6-9 years.\nRegistration required. Please register 
 1 spot for each child attending the workshop.\n***\nAbout this event\nDigi
 tal Expo 2026 is a dynamic day of learning\, exploration and connection fo
 cused on shaping a responsible AI future for everyone.\nFeaturing inspirin
 g speakers and interactive exhibits\, as well as hands-on workshops for ad
 ults\, kids and teens\, the event explores how emerging technologies are t
 ransforming our lives\, communities and civic institutions.\nTogether\, we
 'll examine the opportunities and challenges of AI to foster a more inform
 ed\, inclusive and empowered digital society that protects Canadians and s
 afeguards democracy.\nCheck out tpl.ca/digitalexpo for more information ab
 out the Expo and the workshops.\n***\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe 
 personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Libra
 ry under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). Th
 e information will only be used for event and program registration\, deliv
 ery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your informati
 on can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5
 981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.\n***
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Beeton Hall\, 1st Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a904c8c60ccaf01c02166a2
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
