SUMMARY:Ghost Phenomena: Discoveries of the Searcher Group
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261003T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261003T153000
UID:6aba69feed69cc15475cae2a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Come to learn about true case discoveries\, original theories 
 on life‑after‑life\, tools of the trade\, and rare field photos while 
 debunking common misconceptions about ghosts and how to properly investiga
 te them. Blending chills\, humour\, and a deep respect for Ontario’s dis
 appearing heritage\, this presentation welcomes skeptics\, believers\, and
  the simply curious. Early attendees can enjoy a special pre‑show video 
 at 2:00 pm before the main talk begins at 2:30 pm. Skeptics\, believers an
 d the curious alike are invited to attend this judgment-free event and sta
 y for the Q&A at the end.\nThis program is presented by Peter Roe\, the A
 ssistant Director of The Searcher Group and Director of its subdivision\, 
 Mortal Coil Paranormal. A seasoned investigator\, author\, and advocate fo
 r Ontario’s heritage. Peter is the author of Haunted Town Halls and co
 ‑author of The Complete Paranormal Investigation Handbook.\nDrop in\, no
  registration required.
LOCATION:High Park\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aba69feed69cc15475cae2a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
