X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a904a97be148200298a6e58"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:AI for a Sustainable Future with Digital Moment
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261003T153000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261003T161500
UID:6a904a97be148200298a6e58@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In this parent and caregiver workshop\, participants will lear
 n how AI systems work\, explore how bias can shape outcomes\, and visualiz
 e your digital footprint to better understand technology’s impact on the
  world around you. Through this workshop\, you’ll gain the knowledge and
  confidence to make informed decisions about when\, where and how to use A
 I in everyday life.\n***\nAbout this event\nDigital Expo 2026 is a dynamic
  day of learning\, exploration and connection focused on shaping a respons
 ible AI future for everyone.\nFeaturing inspiring speakers and interactive
  exhibits\, as well as hands-on workshops for adults\, kids and teens\, th
 e event explores how emerging technologies are transforming our lives\, co
 mmunities and civic institutions.\nTogether\, we'll examine the opportunit
 ies and challenges of AI to foster a more informed\, inclusive and empower
 ed digital society that protects Canadians and safeguards democracy.\nChec
 k out tpl.ca/digitalexpo for more information about the Expo and the works
 hops.\n***
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Novella Room\, 2nd Floor (Appel Salon
 )
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a904a97be148200298a6e58
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
