SUMMARY:Geometric Arts and Watercolour
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261005T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261005T200000
UID:6aa6f8a465abe8002a78ea79@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Geometric patterns are among the most recognizable visual expr
 essions of Islamic art and architecture. In the past\, craftsmen had an ex
 tensive practical knowledge of geometry. Nowadays\, we tend to rely heavil
 y on tools such as a protractors\, compasses\, and rulers. In this worksho
 p\, participants will be guided by artist Farooq Zia through step-by-step 
 instructions using drawing tools and watercolour paint to create their own
  geometric pattern and complex design art pieces.\nSpace is limited - regi
 stration is required.
LOCATION:Jane/Sheppard
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa6f8a465abe8002a78ea79
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
