BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-ID:gcal_4h7dspldpuviiv4o1slj9o5p5c
X-SOURCE:CITA Seminars
DTSTART:20261005T190000Z
DTEND:20261005T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20261003T050432Z
UID:i0f1n83c08f0u2q0ghq459k33c@google.com
CREATED:20260727T194443Z
DESCRIPTION:<p>Title: <b>The Variability of Deeply Embedded Protostars: Pas
 t\, Present\, and Future</b></p>\n\n<p>Abstract: Using the James Clerk Maxw
 ell Telescope (JCMT) we have monitored eight nearby low-mass star-forming r
 egions in the Gould\nBelt at submillimetre wavelengths for almost a decade 
 to search for and quantify the time dependent brightness\nvariability of th
 e resident deeply embedded protostars. Secular variability is common among 
 these protostars\; greater\nthan 25% of the sample show measurable long-ter
 m brightness changes and 10% show burst behaviour lasting from months \nto 
 years. We interpret this secular variability as reflecting changes in the m
 ass accretion rate from the disk to the\nprotostar\, as predicted by theore
 tical models of (proto)stellar assembly. For a subset of our sample we have
 \ncontemporaneous mid-IR light-curves which allow additional constraints on
  the conditions responsible for the brightness\nvariations\, confirming tha
 t the submillimetre variability is driven by changes in the dust temperatur
 e profile of the\nenvelope. Furthermore\, we have combined\, for one source
 \, single dish and interferometric sub-mm monitoring\, which\nhas allowed u
 s to unambiguously recover a time lag in the variability at larger angular 
 scales and use the results to\nconfirm the envelope structure surrounding t
 he embedded protostar.</p>\n<p>Host: <b>Shantanu Basu</b></p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260727T194443Z
LOCATION:MP1318A
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Doug Johnstone (DNRC Herzberg)
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
