BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events": "https://events.yorku.ca/events/understanding-and-preventing-burnout/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events
SUMMARY:Understanding and Preventing Burnout
DTSTART:20261006T150000Z
DTEND:20261006T160000Z
DTSTAMP:20260921T222700Z
UID:MEC-3a5a64a567a75090add692e2a4377e8d@events.yorku.ca
RECURRENCE-ID:20261006T150000Z
SEQUENCE:1
CATEGORIES:Well-being,Well-being Week
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260921
DESCRIPTION:Burnout syndrome\, more commonly referred to as burnout\, can 
 affect anyone regardless of gender\, age\, and level of professional respo
 nsibility. Today\, more than ever\, we can better understand this insidiou
 s phenomenon that causes so much individual and collective imbalance. To p
 romote both employee and company well-being\, this workshop highlights the
  causes and factors of burnout\, identifies its physical\, psychological\,
  and behavioural symptoms\, and develops strategies to address it.\nKey Le
 arning Outcomes:\n– Define work-related stress and understand its impact
  on individuals and workplace dynamics.\n– Learn what burnout is\, inclu
 ding its phases\, causes\, and symptoms.\n– Discover strategies to preve
 nt and recover from burnout and promote a healthier work environment.\n–
  Explore various stress management techniques\, such as time management\, 
 relaxation methods\, and visualization exercises.\nOrganized by\n\n\n\n\nO
 rganizational Effectiveness and Well-Being\, Human Resources\n\n\n\n\nForm
 at: Virtual\nAudience: York Staff\nRegister Online\n \n
LAST-MODIFIED:20260921
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
