UID:6a764c428a144f82b2c719ce@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The A(i)\, B's & C's of Artificial Intelligence: The AI Litera
 cy Show\nAn interactive\, multimedia event hosted by Keith McDonald\, Foun
 der of Toronto's the literacyAI project.\nNo technical background required
 .\nDiscover the four specific "need-to-knows" about AI in a fun\, easy-to-
 understand way. Keith uses music\, props\nand video clips to present a com
 pelling case for making AI literacy a must-have in schools and in business
 .\nIncludes presentation and audience Q&A\nThis program is part of Youth H
 ub service. Youth Hubs are a welcoming place for teens after school and in
  the summer\, where helpful staff are always available. Free\, nutritious
  snacks are offered daily. Drop by a branch with a\nYouth Hub\nor call th
 e branch to find out more.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal i
 nformation on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under t
 he Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The informat
 ion will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and ev
 aluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be 
 directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 
 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Malvern\, Youth Hub
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a764c428a144f82b2c719ce
