BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9887195e6fc10d0550f26a"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Author Talk with Dr. Kirsten Johnson on Humanitarienne: A Doctor
 ’s Stories from the Conflict Zone
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261007T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261007T110000
UID:6a9887195e6fc10d0550f26a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:As a physician and public health specialist\,\nDr. Kirsten Joh
 nson\nhas led missions in conflict zones\, disaster-stricken regions and u
 nderserved communities. In her book\,\nHumanitarienne\n: A Doctor's Storie
 s from the Conflict Zone\n\, she traces how a strict childhood marked by t
 rauma pushed her to seek independence early.\nJoin this 1-hour presentatio
 n where Johnson shares her story as a global health expert working in some
  of the world's most volatile places and how she pushed back on inequities
  embedded in humanitarian systems. If you're drawn to international work\,
  social justice\, or the ways in which people are shaped by—and in turn 
 shape the world around them\, this presentation will inspire you.\nJohnson
  will be in conversation with Cindy Schwartz\, a Professional Goal-Centric
   Coach certified through Concordia University.\nPresented as part of Wome
 n's History Month.\nRegistration:\nThis virtual event is free to join and 
 will take place on\nZoom\n.\nRegister to receive an email with details on
  how to join the session and to get a link to the recording.\nCaptions wil
 l be available.\nNeed help with Zoom?\n-\nJoining and participating in a Z
