DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261007T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261007T150000
UID:6a9c556a6562d0229684ec79@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Navigating self-employment in a new country can be challenging
 \, but this workshop will equip newly immigrated entrepreneurs (and new en
 trepreneurs in general) with the essential financial tools to succeed in C
 anada. This workshop is designed to build your confidence in managing your
  business finances and help you thrive as a self-employed professional in 
 Canada. Perfect for newcomers looking to establish a solid financial found
 ation.​\nLimited spots. Registration required.\nThis program is part of 
 Small Business Month.
LOCATION:Maria A. Shchuka\, First Floor Program Room (CPR)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9c556a6562d0229684ec79
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
