SUMMARY:Image Editing for Beginners with Photoshop 1
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261007T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261007T160000
UID:6ab16957ca248a00291759af@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Adobe Photoshop is one of the world’s leading imaging and gr
 aphic design software and is at the core of just about every creative proj
 ect\, from photo editing and compositing to digital painting\, animation\,
  and graphic design.\nJoin us for an introductory lesson and learn about t
 he most common tools. We'll explore the workspace and enhance images while
  investigating tools such as select & mask\, hue & saturation\, layers and
  more. See how an image can be altered and repaired using patch tools such
  as the clone and healing brush tools.\nRegistration is required.\nInforma
 tion Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collecte
 d by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 
 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and
  program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the l
 ibrary handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nan
 swerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Fort York\, Digital Innovation Hub Room 1\, 2nd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab16957ca248a00291759af
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
