SUMMARY:Drop-In Co-op Support (Virtual)
DTSTART:20261007T153000Z
DTEND:20261007T163000Z
DTSTAMP:20261002T145100Z
UID:MEC-ce237f105cfd8a85689cc0481d9d7303@events.yorku.ca__20261007
SEQUENCE:2
CATEGORIES:Co-op &amp\; Career Centre,Co-op Drop-in (CCC),Information Sess
 ions (CCC)
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20261002
DESCRIPTION:Want to connect with a Co-op Coordinator? Join a Co-op Drop-in
 ! It’s the easiest & fastest way to get your questions answered.\nSessio
 n Format: This session is conducted in a group format in order to reduce 
 wait times and to facilitate collaborative and group learning. Breakout ro
 oms are available where students can meet with Co-op Coordinators privatel
 y to discuss specific circumstances. Typically there is a queue for these 
 and we encourage students to join the drop-in time early. To ensure we pro
 vide support to as many students as possible these meetings are from 5-10 
 minutes in duration.\nJoin via Zoom using your PPY York U Log-in account:
  https://yorku.zoom.us/my/askcoop\nHaving trouble logging in? Please mak
 e sure you’re using your PPY York U login. When you select SSO (Single S
 ign-On)\, you should be prompted to sign in with your PPY credentials. If 
 you use a different login\, you may not be able to access the system.\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20261002
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/drop-in-co-op-support-virtual-7/
X-SOURCE:York University
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events": "https://events.yorku.ca/events/construct-an-argument-12/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events
SUMMARY:Construct an Argument
DTSTART:20261007T153000Z
DTEND:20261007T170000Z
DTSTAMP:20260930T173200Z
UID:MEC-2da833ec155de138b47062d56c60fbd8@events.yorku.ca
RECURRENCE-ID:20261007T153000Z
SEQUENCE:3
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/
 09/person-takes-notes-with-pen-and-paper-while.jpg
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Liberal Arts &amp\; Professional Studies,LA&amp\;PS 
 Colleges,LA&amp\;PS Community Hub,LA&amp\;PS Founders College,LA&amp\;PS M
 cLaughlin College,LA&amp\;PS New College,LA&amp\;PS Students All,LA&amp\;P
 S Students-International,LA&amp\;PS Students-Undergrad,LA&amp\;PS Vanier C
 ollege,LA&amp\;PS Writing Centre
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260930
DESCRIPTION:Find out how to make your arguments clear and direct. Enhance 
 your writing by learning to develop a university-level thesis.\nThe Write 
 Now! series consists of four workshops\, each of which focuses on one aspe
 ct of the writing process:\nWorkshop 1: Analyze Your Assignment\nWorkshop 
 2: Construct an Argument\nWorkshop 3: Meaningful Citations\nWorkshop 4: Ef
 fective Editing\nAt the end of each workshop\, you’ll receive access to 
 a quiz\, which you will need to complete within 72 hours of the workshop d
 ate. If you pass the quiz\, you will receive a badge\, which will be recor
 ded on the Write Now! eClass site.\nIf you attend all four workshops and p
 ass each workshop’s quiz within one academic calendar year\, you’ll at
 tain a Certificate of Completion that can be added to your resume and prof
 essional networking sites\, such as LinkedIn.\nClick to authenticate and j
 oin!\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20260930
ORGANIZER;CN="Writing Centre":MAILTO:jroberts@yorku.ca, dbaus@yorku.ca, la
 pswrit@yorku.ca
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/construct-an-argument-12/
X-SOURCE:York University
END:VEVENT
