SUMMARY:Youth Hub: Hacking Social Media
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261007T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261007T170000
UID:6abe8d6c377296003a48ebb6@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Keith McDonald\, founder of the literacy AI project\, shares h
 is\nseven rules for\nhaving fun with social media\n. Following these rules
  allows audiences to gain control over algorithms and learn how to recogni
 ze and deal with the social pressures\, bullying\, and reputational implic
 ations of social media use. The presentation also includes how to identify
  and reduce security and privacy risks. This is a multi-media presentation
  featuring video clips\, props\, and group discussions\, and it begins wit
 h an opening social media song icebreaker.\nDrop-In program\, no registrat
 ion.\nThis program is part of Youth Hub service. Youth Hubs are a welcomin
 g place for teens after school and in the summer\, where helpful staff are
  always available. Free\, nutritious snacks are offered daily. Drop by a
  branch with a\nYouth Hub\nor call the branch to find out more.
LOCATION:Woodside Square\, Multi-purpose Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abe8d6c377296003a48ebb6
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
