BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events": "https://events.yorku.ca/events/co-op-information-session/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events
SUMMARY:Co-op Information Session (Online)
DTSTART:20261007T180000Z
DTEND:20261007T193000Z
DTSTAMP:20260824T182500Z
UID:MEC-1951440c60517e1646b22e78584305b1@events.yorku.ca
RECURRENCE-ID:20261007T180000Z
SEQUENCE:3
CATEGORIES:Co-op &amp\; Career Centre,Co-op Mandatory Sessions (CCC),Infor
 mation Sessions (CCC)
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260824
DESCRIPTION:\nYork U Co-op Information Session (live webinar)\nLocation: O
 nline\nDate: October 7\, 2026\nTime: 2:00pm-3:30pm\nThe York University 
 Co-op Program provides students with opportunities for paid\, hands-on lea
 rning and valuable industry experience. We encourage you to visit the Co-o
 perative Education website to review program details and confirm that you 
 meet the academic requirements.\nDuring this session\, you will learn abou
 t:\n\nThe co-op advantage\nEligibility requirements\nProgram fees\nThe reg
 istration process\nGeneral Q&A with a Co-op Coordinator\n\nThese sessions 
 are available in three formats to support your schedule and learning prefe
 rences:\n\nIn-person\nLive webinar (Zoom)\nSelf-paced online modules thro
 ugh the Lassonde Co-op Preparatory Course (eClass)\n\nTarget Audience:\nYo
 rk U students intending to begin their first co-op work term in Summer 20
 27. Before registering\, please self-assess your eligibility for the prog
 ram\nLive Session vs. Self-Paced Modules: What’s the Difference?\nBased 
 on student feedback\, we now offer flexible options to complete the requir
 ed sessions. Each format has unique benefits:\n\nLive sessions (in-person 
 or webinar): Opportunity to ask questions and interact directly with a Co
 -op Coordinator.\nSelf-paced eClass modules: Complete the content at a ti
 me that is most convenient for you.\n\nImportant Reminders:\n\nRequired se
 ssions must be completed for your application to be reviewed.\nAlready att
 ended a mandatory session within the last 12 months? You do not need to at
 tend again.\nAlready admitted to Co-op? You are not required to complete t
 he mandatory sessions or re-apply.\n\nIf you have an eligible work term fo
 r Summer 2027: Log in to the co-op portal and accept the terms and conditi
 ons when prompted.\n\n\n\nWe look forward to your participation!\nRegister
  Here [icon name=”chevron-right” class=”small pl-2″]\nAccessibilit
 y\nIf you require accommodations\, please contact askcoop@yorku.ca\, and 
 a member of our team will follow up with you.\nCode of Conduct\nBefore att
 ending\, please review the Code of Rights and Responsibilities from the 
 York University Office of Student Community Relations to help ensure a res
 pectful and positive experience for all participants.\nGuests who exhibit 
 behaviour that violates this code may be removed from the event. If you ex
 perience behaviour that does not align with these expectations\, please co
 ntact our team at askcoop@yorku.ca.\nHaving trouble logging in? \nPlease
  make sure you’re using your PPY York U login. When you select SSO (Sing
 le Sign-On)\, you should be prompted to sign in with your PPY credentials.
  If you use a different login\, you may not be able to access the system.\
 n
LAST-MODIFIED:20261002
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/co-op-information-session/
X-SOURCE:York University
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Gcal 3Oo6S709Gu7D31Cg1419Cfrbuc": "https://luma.com/51wvawbd"}
X-SOURCE-ID:gcal_3oo6s709gu7d31cg1419cfrbuc
SUMMARY:Nerd Show & Tell
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261007T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261007T210000
DTSTAMP:20261003T050439Z
UID:6A35ED33-7C70-4C6A-A14E-394A628B436C
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Toronto:20261007T180000
SEQUENCE:0
CREATED:20260911T183236Z
DESCRIPTION:It is easier to talk about your projects and what you want to 
 learn than build something that real integrates into people's lives. Eithe
 r show up and demo what you are building or come over\, try what other peo
 ple are building\, give your feedback\, get inspired\, and learn something
 . Why talk about what can be when you can be the change you want to see in
  the world?\n\n​Change requires knowledge\, skills\, and coordination. W
 ith all this information at our fingertips knowing what to ignore is more 
 important than knowing what one should know. My bet is that we can achieve
  more together than alone.\n\n​So let's get our values articulated\, so 
 we can converse\, and build a future worth getting excited about!
LAST-MODIFIED:20260912T200100Z
LOCATION:HackLab.TO\n1677 St Clair Ave W\, Toronto ON M6N 1H9\, Canada
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
