SUMMARY:Introduction to Gemini Notebook
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261007T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261007T190000
UID:6aa42baaf9ed2e00384fd806@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Get started with Gemini Notebook\, a free AI-powered tool to h
 elp organize information and generate summaries (including audio and video
  summaries) based on your own sources (eg textbooks\, websites\, reports\,
  codebases\, literature\, videos etc) We'll also discuss the basics of h
 ow AI generates text\, strategies for evaluating information\, protecting
  privacy\, and using AI responsibly.\nA Google account is required to save
  your work. Staff will not be able to assist with account creation during
  the program. You are welcome to attend without a Google account.\nRegistr
 ation is recommended\, but we will accommodate drop-ins.\nInformation Co
 llection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by th
 e Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\,
  20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and progra
 m registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library 
 handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerlin
 e@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Main Floor\, Learning Center 2
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa42baaf9ed2e00384fd806
