DESCRIPTION:Human connection has a profound impact on our health and happi
 ness\, especially in our increasingly disconnected world. Join GenWell in 
 an interactive 5-week program series to learn practical ways to enhance so
 cial health\, understand the adverse effects of loneliness\, and discover 
 the benefits of building more meaningful connections. Receive a free socia
 l health workbook\, spend time with other participants after the workshops
 \, and enjoy some light refreshments provided.\nAbout GenWell: Founded in 
 2016\, GenWell is a registered charity whose mission is to make the world 
 a happier and healthier place by educating\, empowering\, and catalyzing f
 orty million Canadians about the importance of their social health.\nRegis
 tration required. *Participants are encouraged to attend every session*\n
 Information Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is c
 ollected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, se
 ctions 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for ev
 ent and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about ho
 w the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff
  at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4
 W 2G8.
LOCATION:Fairview\, Room 201
