BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events": "https://events.yorku.ca/events/leader-dialogue-from-tension-to-teamwork-for-people-managers/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events
SUMMARY:Leader Dialogue: From Tension to Teamwork (for people managers)
DTSTART:20261008T140000Z
DTEND:20261008T153000Z
DTSTAMP:20260915T193700Z
UID:MEC-febb75eccd1101d84a2aa5eb87859ce0@events.yorku.ca
RECURRENCE-ID:20261008T140000Z
SEQUENCE:1
CATEGORIES:Well-being,Well-being Week
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260915
DESCRIPTION:Tension and conflict are a normal part of working relationship
 s—especially during change\, high workload\, or moments of unclear expec
 tations. What matters most is not avoiding conflict\, but how managers rec
 ognize it early\, respond productively\, and use it to strengthen trust an
 d performance. This interactive 90 minute session helps people managers bu
 ild confidence and capability in navigating tension and everyday conflict.
  Managers will practice practical tools for addressing misunderstandings\,
  surfacing differing perspectives\, and resetting strained relationships
 —before issues escalate or harden. Through discussion\, reflection\, and
  real world scenarios\, participants will leave better equipped to move te
 ams from friction to forward progress.\nKey Learning Outcomes:\n– Refram
 e tension in times of change as a typical and workable dynamic\, and diffe
 rentiate healthy tension from unresolved conflict or relationship breakdow
 n.\n– Identify personal and team conflict patterns by noticing early sig
 ns of tension\, common triggers\, and default responses\, and understandin
 g how these patterns show up during periods of change.\n– Apply practica
 l conversation tools to address tensions respectfully—surfacing concerns
 \, naming impact\, inviting perspective\, and leading reset conversations 
 that maintain shared expectations without blame or escalation.\nOrganized 
 by Organizational Effectiveness and Well-Being\, Human Resources\nFormat: 
 Virtual\nAudience: York University People Managers and HR professionals\n
 Register Online\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20260915
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/leader-dialogue-from-tension-to-teamwor
 k-for-people-managers/
X-SOURCE:York University
END:VEVENT
