DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261008T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261008T183000
SUMMARY:ROTMAN Author Talk:  Power of Situations
DESCRIPTION:TORONTO ARTS & CULTURE\nWe attend various ROTMAN events each y
 ear. Author Talks. Book Releases. Visiting Professors.\n\n### **Agenda:**\
 n\n5:00 pm - Check-in opens + light refreshments\n5:30 pm - Author present
 ation and moderated Q&A\n6:30 pm - Meet-and-greet with author + book signi
 ng\n\n### **Book Synopsis:**\n\n**From the #1 bestselling author of *Grit\
 ,* a new book that reveals the hidden power of situations—and how you ca
 n shape them to bring out your best.**\n\nAngela Duckworth\, PhD\, is the 
 bestselling author of *Grit* and the founder and CEO of Character Lab. A 2
 013 MacArthur Fellow\, she is a professor of psychology at the University 
 of Pennsylvania.\n\n**In Angela Duckworth’s first book\, she showed that
  a common denominator of successful strivers is a blend of passion and per
 severance she dubbed “grit.**”\n\nTicket link is below. $22-$45\n\nThi
 s second book springs from her deepening realization that grit\, while nec
 essary\, is sometimes not sufficient. How you situate yourself to meet a c
 hallenge can be crucial.\nDuckworth’s in-depth research reveals the enor
 mous influence wielded by the objects within arm’s reach\, your peers an
 d mentors\, and even your zip code. Though you’re often told to make the
  best of your situation\, it is far\, far better to make your situation be
 tter first.\n\n**In *Situated*\, you’ll discover:**\n\n* Why your person
 ality changes\, sometimes dramatically\, from one situation to another—a
 nd how you can harness that shift\n* The secret to conquering temptation *
 without* willpower\n* Why taking the less effortful path can feel like che
 ating but often solves a stubborn problem\n* How the company you keep shap
 es the person you become\n* The most effective ways to help others succeed
 \n\n***TICKET Link here-***-\n\nhttps://www.rotman.utoronto.ca/news-events
 -and-ideas/public-events/events-listings/2026/october-2026/oct-8---angela-
 duckworth/
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/toronto-arts-and-culture/events/31497
 4584/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260527T101544Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260527T101544Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
