SUMMARY:Key Ingredients for Child and Family Well-Being
DTSTART:20261008T173000Z
DTEND:20261008T183000Z
DTSTAMP:20260917T184800Z
UID:MEC-1895037c0fa55110b0e0e20d2e68a0d7@events.yorku.ca
RECURRENCE-ID:20261008T173000Z
SEQUENCE:3
CATEGORIES:Well-being,Well-being Week
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260917
DESCRIPTION:\n\n\n\nFamily life can be rewarding – but it can also be ch
 allenging\, particularly when work\, school\, and other demands compete fo
 r our time and attention. Join Dr. Heather Prime\, a child psychologist\, 
 and Gillian Shoychet\, a clinical-developmental doctoral student\, from th
 e York University Psychology Clinic for an engaging\, research-informed se
 ssion exploring the key ingredients for fostering family and child well-be
 ing. We will discuss how family stress can affect relationships and what h
 elps parents work effectively as a team. We will also explore skills for s
 upporting children’s emotional and behavioural well-being\, including em
 otion coaching and other evidence-informed parenting strategies. The sessi
 on will conclude by highlighting some of the family-focused supports avail
 able through the York University Psychology Clinic.\n\n\n\n\n\nOrganized b
 y Department of Psychology\nFormat: Virtual\nAudience: York Community\nZo
 om Link\n\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20260917
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/key-ingredients-for-child-and-family-we
 ll-being/
