X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Gardinermuseum": "https://www.gardinermuseum.on.ca/event/hand-building-and-surface-design-stoneware-all-levels-fall-2026/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:gardinermuseum
X-SOURCE:Gardiner Museum
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261008T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261126T203000
DTSTAMP:20260805T182841Z
CREATED:20260805T182841Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260805T182841Z
UID:146350-1791480600-1795725000@www.gardinermuseum.on.ca
SUMMARY:Hand Building and Surface Design: Stoneware (All Levels)
DESCRIPTION:Hand Building and Surface Design: Stoneware (All Levels)            \n                                \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n	\n\n	\n\n\n			\nEvents\n	\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n	\n\n	\n\n	\n\n\n				\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n	\n\n\n			\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Thursdays October 8 to November 26\, 2026\n5:30 pm – 8:30 pm\n \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    \nFor ages 18+ \nBring an illustrative quality to your ceramics by exploring a variety of contemporary approaches to surface design. Learn about underglaze painting\, inlay (mishima)\, sgraffito\, stencils\, and more. This 8-week class is designed for all levels—beginners are welcome\, but be ready to push yourself. \n\nThis class includes access to a 10kg bag of clay\, glazes and underglazes. Additional bags can be purchased for $35 each. \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n	\n\n\n\n\n			\n\n        \n          \n          \n                        \n               \n                Gardiner Friends : $434\n                                        \n                        \n               \n                General : $510\n                                        \n                      \n\n           \n            \n              Gardiner Friends\, log in to access your discount.* \nNot a Gardiner Friend yet? Join now at the Friend level or above to save . \n*Discounts on programs and classes do not apply to ‘Annual Pass’ level. \n            \n                    \n          \n            \n  \n            \n                \n                                    Add to cart\n\n                    \n\n\n                \n                            \n           \n                \n                \n                    \n                        \n                    \n                \n                \n          \n          \n        \n\n	\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Class dates: October 8\, 15\, 22\, 29\, November 5\, 12\, 19\, 26\n \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Class Outline: \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Week 1: Make 5 -6 small pinch pots or plates\nWeek 2: Intro to underglaze\nWeek 3: Intro to inlay methods\nWeek 4: Intro to sgraffito and revealing inlay designs\nWeek 5: Intro to stencils and transfers\nWeek 6: Intro to marbling\nWeek 7: Trimming and finishing pieces\nWeek 8: Glazing \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Important Information: \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    \nPlease ensure the course you choose works with your schedule. For any withdrawals\, a non-refundable fee of $50 fee per course will be charged\, regardless of the reason for withdrawal. Withdrawals will not be accepted for any reason within 10 business days prior to the program start date or after the program has begun.\nBy signing up for this class\, participants are committing to abide by the Museum’s Code of Conduct\, Ticketing Policy\, and Studio Policy.\n\nGardiner Friends\, please log in to access your discount and front-of-the-line access. Gardiner Friends may only purchase adult clay classes at the discounted rate for membership card holders. \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n                       \n            \n                \n                    Instructor\n                    \n                \n                \n                    Misbah Ahmed\n                    \n                \n                \n                    Misbah Ahmed is a Toronto-based multidisciplinary artist working primarily in painting\, ceramic sculpture\, and printmaking. Her art merges research on historical non-Western crafts and artifacts with a dedication to environmental themes\, reflecting her growing concern for ecological issues. Misbah completed a Bachelor of Design in Illustration from OCAD University in 2018\, where she received the program medal. \n                            \n            \n        \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         
URL:https://www.gardinermuseum.on.ca/event/hand-building-and-surface-design-stoneware-all-levels-fall-2026/
LOCATION:Gardiner Museum\, 111 Queen's Park\, Toronto\, ON\, M5S 2C7\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Adult Classes
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.gardinermuseum.on.ca/wp-content/uploads/Surface-Decoration-Thumbnail-Fall-2026.jpg
GEO:43.6679938;-79.3935128
