SUMMARY:Reschedule:  Artists in the Library:  Woodland Sunflower Felt Coll
 age
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261008T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261008T200000
UID:6a7e5d66b20478002992c363@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Part 1 of a series of workshops for adults\, exploring local f
 lora through embroidery and felt collage.  This event is part of the\nAr
 tists in the Library\nprogram\, hosted by Artist\, Sarah Zanchetta.\nRegis
 tration is required. Space is limited.\nPlease note: Registered participan
 t spaces will be held for 15 minutes after which drop-ins will be allowed.
 \nPlease note: This is a rescheduled program originally from Wed\, Sept 30
 \, then a reschedule from the Oct 1st\, 2026 date - our apologies for the
  inconvenience.\nMeet the Resident:\nSarah Zanchetta (she/they) is a queer
  textile artist and educator whose practice dives into the loss of connect
 ion and knowledge of poisonous plants in North America. Zanchetta uses tex
 tiles\, texts\, and hosts community workshops to create intimate works and
  spaces where we can unfold our curiosities\, care and anxieties about wha
 t grows beside our feet. She holds a Master of Visual Studies from the Un
 iversity of Toronto (2023) and a BFA from OCAD University (2018).\nInforma
 tion Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collecte
 d by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 
 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and
  program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the l
 ibrary handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nan
 swerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Mount Dennis\, Room 2
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a7e5d66b20478002992c363
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
