SUMMARY:Makers Making Change: Exploring Accessibility Technology
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261008T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261008T193000
UID:6aa3335e101eb7003f2f24bb@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This workshop is offered in English with themes on accessibili
 ty\, inclusion\, and accessible resources. This interactive workshop explo
 res how community makers are improving accessibility through open-source a
 ssistive technology. Participants will learn about the\nNeil Squire Societ
 y’s\nlocal device library\, how it supports people with disabilities\, a
 nd how free\, customizable tools are designed and shared.\nThe session inc
 ludes a hands-on showcase of 3D-printed assistive devices and an interacti
 ve discussion on inclusive design and everyday problem-solving. Open to pe
 ople of all abilities\, no technical experience required.\nThe presenter o
 f this workshop will be from the\nNeil Squire Society\n.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 101
