BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Torontobotanicalgarden": "https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/event/tafelmusik-at-the-garden-voices-of-the-violin/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:torontobotanicalgarden
X-SOURCE:Toronto Botanical Garden
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261008T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261008T200000
DTSTAMP:20261003T010544
CREATED:20260909T153856Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260922T194857Z
UID:10002031-1791486000-1791489600@torontobotanicalgarden.ca
SUMMARY:Tafelmusik at the Garden: Voices of the Violin
DESCRIPTION:Voices of the Violin explores the astonishing range of the unaccompanied violin across more than three centuries. Stripped of accompaniment\, a single instrument becomes many: storyteller\, dancer\, orator\, and virtuoso by turns. The program moves from the concise\, improvisatory gestures of 17th- and 18th-century preludes and dances—by Corbett\, Purcell\, Lonati\, Telemann\, Vitali\, Jacquet de La Guerre\, and Vilsmaÿr—to the monumental unaccompanied works of Biber and Bach\, before Andrew Balfour carries that same solitary voice into the present day. Across four centuries\, the question remains constant: how can four strings speak with so many voices? \nThursday\, October 8\, 7 p.m.\nPublic $25\, TBG Members and Tafelmusik Subscribers $23 (plus fees and HST)Indoor ConcertGeneral Admission Seating. \nGroup Sales\nBring your group of 10 or more to this event and take advantage of great savings. For more information on Group Sales\, please contact info@torontobotanicalgarden.ca. \nAccessible Seating\nAccessible seating is available in the hall. Please contact us in advance so we can better assist you\, and/or arrive early for priority seating before the hall is open to the public. For more information on Accessible Seating\, please contact info@torontobotanicalgarden.ca. \nSupport Person\nThe support person who accompanies a patron with special needs is eligible for a complimentary ticket/admission. Support person tickets/admission are subject to availability. For more information on Accessible Services at our venues or support persons\, please contact info@torontobotanicalgarden.ca. \nAbout Tafelmusik\nEvery now and then a group of musicians comes along and changes the way we think about music. For over four decades\, Tafelmusik has been synonymous worldwide with dynamic\, engaging\, and soulful performances informed by scholarship\, passion and artistic excellence. \nPerforming on instruments and in styles appropriate to the era\, Tafelmusik has performed in more than 350 cities in 32 countries. Its extensive discography on the Sony\, CBC Records\, Analekta and Tafelmusik Media labels have garnered ten JUNOs and numerous international recording prizes. From a vibrant home season in Toronto\, to international tours\, award-winning recordings\, innovative collaborations\, and inspiring education programs\, Tafelmusik is a musical powerhouse with a reputation for thrilling and delighting audiences. www.tafelmusik.org \nBecome a TBG Member\nJoin the Toronto Botanical Garden as a member to receive a discount on this program\, upcoming events and classes\, and free parking. A Toronto Botanical Garden membership helps you deepen your knowledge and connection to the natural world\, become a part of a dynamic community of plant people\, and be inspired! \nBecome a member. \n\nTo learn more about what we’re doing to make your next visit safe\, enriching\, and uplifting\, please review our list of Frequently Asked Questions.\nThis is an in-person\, indoor program at the Toronto Botanical Garden.
URL:https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/event/tafelmusik-at-the-garden-voices-of-the-violin/
CATEGORIES:Tafelmusik
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/b248fa8552dc48ab6ff7dc5bd5975974.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
