BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Gardinermuseum": "https://www.gardinermuseum.on.ca/event/after-the-island-public-opening/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:gardinermuseum
X-SOURCE:Gardiner Museum
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261008T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261008T210000
DTSTAMP:20260928T150330Z
CREATED:20260908T215318Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260928T150330Z
UID:147135-1791487800-1791493200@www.gardinermuseum.on.ca
SUMMARY:After the Island: Public Opening
DESCRIPTION:After the Island: Public Opening            \n                                    \n                                \n                        \n                                                \n                                                        Free Registration                        \n                                            \n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n	\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n	\n\n\n			\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Thursday October 8\, 2026\n7:30 pm – 9:00 pm\nFree with registration \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Celebrate the opening of After the Island: Caribbean Canadian Ceramics\, a landmark curatorial partnership with Black Artists’ Networks in Dialogue (BAND) and the Museum of the African Diaspora (MoAD)\, exploring contemporary ceramic practices rooted in Caribbean histories\, memory\, and cultural transformation. \nJoin the artists and curators for evening of art\, music\, and community\, with drinks available for purchase. \nRegistration is required as capacity is limited. \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n	\n\n\n\n\n			\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    \nSold Out \n\n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n        \n          \n          \n                        \n               \n                General : Free\n                                        \n                        \n                                        \n                      \n\n                    \n          \n            \n  \n            \n              \n                        \n           \n                \n                \n                    \n                        \n                    \n                \n                \n          \n          \n        \n\n	\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    About the Exhibition \nThe Gardiner Museum\, Black Artists’ Networks in Dialogue (BAND)\, and the Museum of the African Diaspora (MoAD) present a landmark curatorial partnership exploring contemporary ceramic practices rooted in Caribbean histories\, memory\, and cultural transformation. After the Island: Caribbean Canadian Ceramics considers how artists of the Caribbean diaspora are embracing the medium of ceramics to explore themes of knowledge transfer and the liberatory potential of the clandestine. Through existing and new work by Caribbean Canadian artists PJ Anderson\, Eddy Firmin\, Manuel Mathieu\, and Sharon Norwood\, the exhibition approaches questions of identity\, belonging\, memory\, and cultural continuity through the language of clay. Learn more \n  \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n\n  \n              \n                    \n                Exhibition Partners\n                \n                                \n                            \n            \n  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n              \n                    \n                Presenting Sponsors\n                \n                                \n                            \n                    \n                Supporting Partners\n                \n                                \n                            \n            \n  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n              \n                    \n                Government Support\n                \n                                \n                                \n                            \n                    \n                Project Partner\n                \n                                \n                            \n            \n  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n              \n                    \n                Media Partners\n                \n                                \n                                \n                            \n            \n  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n              \n                    \n                Hospitality Partner\n                \n                                \n                            \n            \n  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n              \n                    \n                Thanks To\n                \n                                \n                            \n            \n  \n\n\n\n\n\n    \n         
URL:https://www.gardinermuseum.on.ca/event/after-the-island-public-opening/
LOCATION:Gardiner Museum\, 111 Queen's Park\, Toronto\, ON\, M5S 2C7\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Programs & Events
