DESCRIPTION:Are you a musician\, poet\, or storyteller? If so\, then you a
 re invited to share your talents at the Lillian H. Smith Library Open Mic!
 \nPlease note: stand-up comedy is not featured. Only music\, poetry\, and 
 storytelling.\nThis program is for adults and seniors. 5 minutes provided
  for each performance.\nFor musicians\, please bring your music instrument
 (s) and/or backing track(s).\nPerformers sign up at 5:30pm.\nFor more info
 rmation\, please contact Lillian H. Smith Library at 416-393-7746.\n***\nA
 ccessibility at Toronto Public Library:\nToronto Public Library is committ
 ed to accessibility. Please call or email us if you are Deaf or have a dis
 ability and would like to request accommodation to participate in this pro
 gram. Please let us know as far in advance as possible and we will do our 
 best to meet your request. At least three weeks notice is preferred. Phone
  416-393-7099 or email accessibleservices@tpl.ca.
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith\, Basement (Room BC)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a90c7f82dac6e0037223ec9
