X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_thescifibookclub
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Sci Fi Book Club
UID:event_316773246@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261003T050446Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261009T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261009T210000
SUMMARY:Friday Night Frights @ Brooklyn SciFi Festival
DESCRIPTION:The Sci Fi Book Club\nHi everybody!\n\n[Brooklyn SciFi Film Fe
 stival](https://brooklynscififilmfest.com/) presents an evening of SciFi/H
 orror films curated by the masters of macabre at Brooklyn Horror Film Fest
 ival to be hosted at Stuart Cinema\, Friday\, October 9th from 7:00 to 9:0
 0. Our first-time crossover event is sure to please fans of both science f
 iction and horror as we present a program of seven short films in Long Isl
 and City (Queens). Join us at 6:30 for a cocktail mixer before the event.\
 n\n**[Purchase your tickets for this event via Eventbrite](https://www.eve
 ntbrite.com/e/friday-night-frights-scifi-horror-night-tickets-200050622697
 7?aff=ebdsshcopyurl&utm-campaign=social&utm-content=attendeeshare&utm-medi
 um=discovery&utm-term=creator-collections&utm-share-source=creator-collect
 ions )\, your rsvp to this Meetup event is not enough.** Get your tickets 
 asap if you're interested\, this event will sell out!\n\n**Use the code SI
 FIBookClubBSF26 for 15% off.**\n\nThe festival has highlighted hundreds of
  bold voices in the genre\, and we're back for our seventh annual program\
 , showcasing more than 200 films from around the world. BSFFF will run Oct
 ober 5–18\, 2026\, streaming online and at in-person events the 5th-11th
  across Brooklyn.\n\nHope to see you there!\nCheers\, Jon & Meghan
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/thescifibookclub/events/316773246/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260930T010021Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260930T010021Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Aga Khan Museum": "https://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/lamhe/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:agakhan_museum
SUMMARY:Lamhe
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261009T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261009T193000
UID:lamhe-2026-10-09t19-30-00-04-00@agakhanmuseum.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://images.agakhanmuseum.org/uploads/2026/09
 /Lamhe_1-aspect-ratio-1600-1000.jpg?resize=1584%2C990&gravity
DESCRIPTION:Some stories are ahead of their time. Some become timeless.\n\
 nThe Aga Khan Museum is proud to partner with Classic Legends Indian Films
  Festival (CLIFF) — a celebration of Indian cinema\, bringing together t
 imeless classics\, acclaimed contemporary films\, distinguished filmmakers
 \, and engaging conversations. The festival honours India’s rich cinemat
 ic legacy while creating a global platform for screenings\, retrospectives
 \, cultural exchange\, and dialogue between cinema\, literature\, and the 
 performing arts.\n\nAs part of CLIFF 2026\, audiences are invited to redis
 cover Lamhe on the big screen and experience a film whose ideas about love
 \, relationships and changing social expectations continue to invite conve
 rsation.
LOCATION:Aga Khan Museum\, 77 Wynford Drive\, Toronto\, ON M3C 1K1
URL:https://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/lamhe/
X-SOURCE:Aga Khan Museum
END:VEVENT
