BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Microsoft Reactor Toronto": "https://www.meetup.com/microsoft-reactor-toronto/events/315976012/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_microsoft_reactor_toronto
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Microsoft Reactor Toronto
UID:event_315976012@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261003T050444Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261013T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261013T120000
SUMMARY:Agents That Take Action: Secure Enterprise Integration with Azure
DESCRIPTION:Microsoft Reactor Toronto\nAn enterprise agent becomes genuine
 ly useful when it can act on business systems. It also becomes significant
 ly more dangerous if those integrations are not governed correctly.\n\nIn 
 this session\, we will connect our Microsoft Foundry agent to real enterpr
 ise capabilities using Azure API Management\, Azure Logic Apps\, Azure Fun
 ctions\, Azure Service Bus\, OpenAPI tools\, and Model Context Protocol se
 rvers.\n\nThe agent will create an incident ticket\, initiate an approval 
 workflow\, invoke a protected business API\, submit a long-running remedia
 tion command\, and report the final result back to the user. Rather than a
 llowing the model direct access to backend systems\, we will introduce a g
 overned integration layer with typed tool contracts\, authentication\, aut
 horization\, rate limiting\, schema validation\, retries\, and centralized
  logging.\n\nWe will also compare the roles of OpenAPI tools\, MCP servers
 \, Logic Apps actions\, Azure Functions\, and asynchronous messaging. Mana
 ged identities and Microsoft Entra ID will be used to eliminate embedded A
 PI keys and apply least-privilege access across the solution.\n\nBy the en
 d of the session\, attendees will understand how to give agents meaningful
  enterprise capabilities without bypassing security\, integration governan
 ce\, or operational controls. Key topics: Microsoft Foundry tools OpenAPI 
 and Model Context Protocol Azure API Management as an AI gateway Azure Log
 ic Apps agent actions Azure Functions Azure Service Bus Managed identity a
 nd Microsoft Entra ID Secure and asynchronous tool execution.\n\n---------
 -----------------------------------------------------\n\nThis session is a
  part of a series\, learn more here! [https://aka.ms/ProBadgeSeries-TY](ht
 tps://aka.ms/ProBadgeSeries-TY)\n\n[eventID:27509]
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/microsoft-reactor-toronto/events/3159
 76012/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260804T161055Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260804T161055Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
