BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Young Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aad8927101eb7003f31390c"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_young_adults
SUMMARY:Democracy Fitness: Active Listening
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261013T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261013T130000
UID:6aad8927101eb7003f31390c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Develop and exercise the skills you need to be an active parti
 cipant in everyday democracy in this fun\, interactive\nsession. Democracy
  Fitness expands traditional ideas of what democracy is by exploring the s
 kills that help people participate in civic life\, build understanding and
  work together.\nIn this session\, we’ll exercise our\nActive Listening\
 nmuscles. In a democracy\, everyone has the right to speak. Being heard re
 quires that someone listens. When you listen openly and with curiosity\, y
 ou create understanding and trust.\nThis program is for\nadults\,\nplease 
 register for email reminders\, drop-in's are welcome.\nThis program is off
 ered in partnership with Democracy Fitness Global and MASS LBP.\nGenerousl
 y supported by McConnell Foundation.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe 
 personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Libra
 ry under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). Th
 e information will only be used for event and program registration\, deliv
 ery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your informati
 on can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5
 981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Malvern
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aad8927101eb7003f31390c
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
