X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events": "https://events.yorku.ca/events/modes-of-delivery-intensive-redesigning-the-mode-of-course-delivery-for-authentic-assessment-online-oct-13/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events
SUMMARY:Modes of Delivery Intensive: (Re)Designing the Mode of Course Deli
 very for Authentic Assessment (Online\, Oct. 13)
DTSTART:20261013T133000Z
DTEND:20261013T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20260903T142100Z
UID:MEC-f8207ff936432245e67f23f6d8f7db1a@events.yorku.ca
RECURRENCE-ID:20261013T133000Z
SEQUENCE:6
CATEGORIES:Faculty Affairs,Teaching &amp\; Learning
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260903
DESCRIPTION:Generative Artificial Intelligence (GenAI) has made take-home 
 and online assessment unreliable. Rethinking entire course assessment stra
 tegies that address this challenge and align with the mode of course deliv
 ery is the focus of this intensive.\nThe modes of delivery intensive is a 
 full day\, virtual event that includes sharing innovative ideas for course
  design across each mode of delivery (in-person\, blended\, online). Parti
 cipants will engage in a process of making deep\, substantive\, robust cha
 nges to their courses\, assessments\, or teaching practices.\nRegister via
  YULearn (requires Passport York login)\n*Please note\, if you are unable
  to register via Passport York (e.g. you are in between contracts\, or a p
 articipant external to York) register via Zoom\nMore information is avail
 able on the Teaching Commons Website.\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20260914
LOCATION:Online via Zoom.
ORGANIZER;CN="Teaching Commons":MAILTO:teaching@yorku.ca
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/modes-of-delivery-intensive-redesigning
 -the-mode-of-course-delivery-for-authentic-assessment-online-oct-13/
X-SOURCE:York University
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa057f5648f481be43addb2"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Start & Grow Your Business with TSBEC
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261013T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261013T150000
UID:6aa057f5648f481be43addb2@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Information session on how to start\, plan\, finance and grow 
 your very own small business.\nOwning a business is a dream for many peopl
 e. Every new business starts with an idea. This interactive presentation w
 ill give an overview of how to make it happen and the opportunity to ask q
 uestions related to your business. An advisor from TSBEC (Toronto Small Bu
 siness Enterprise Centre\, formerly Enterprise Toronto) will present an ov
 erview of information related to the business planning process\, evaluatin
 g a business idea\, financing\, marketing planning\, business structures\,
  regulatory requirements\, and more.
LOCATION:Jane/Sheppard
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa057f5648f481be43addb2
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa464b886d8450031156f86"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Google Prompting Essentials: Online Learning Circle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261013T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261013T160000
UID:6aa464b886d8450031156f86@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Ready to develop the skills to use generative AI (GenAI) tools
  effectively and responsibly for work and daily life? Join our staff-facil
 itated Learning Circle to complete the self-paced Google Prompting special
 ization. By completing this Learning Circle program\, you will earn a Goo
 gle Prompting Essentials certificate to share on your resume\, LinkedIn an
 d social media profiles!\nWhat You'll Learn\nThis program is designed for 
 those with some experience with using GenAI. Through short videos\, articl
 es\, assignments and quizzes\, you will discover:\nEssential\nPrompting Sk
 ills\n: How to use a prompting framework to create a desired output with G
 enAI\; how to evaluate and refine your results.\nEveryday Work Tasks:\nStr
 ategies to draft content\, brainstorm ideas\, create tables\, timelines\, 
 and more.\nData & Presentations:\nHow to explore data visualization and us
 e GenAI responsibly when working with data.\nAdvanced Techniques:\nHow to 
 use prompt chaining for complex tasks and prompt versioning to save and re
 use your best prompts over time.\nLearning Circles are study groups guided
  by\nlibrary staff for people who want to complete the Google Prompting sp
 ecialization together in a welcoming space:\nLearners meet weekly and work
  together through course materials.\nParticipants are expected to commit t
 o attending all four Learning Circle sessions.\nSome Experience with GenAI
  Recommended: This course is ideal for participants who have completed the
  AI Essentials course Learning Circle.\nHow to Joi\nn a Learning Circle:\n
 Register once for the first session of this event series\, in order to att
 end all sessions.\nPlease sign up with a valid email address.\nA valid TPL
  library card is required for online circles.\nAttend all four sessions 
 online via Zoom\, on\nTuesdays October 6\, 13\, 20\, 27 from 1:30-4pm.\nR
 egistration is a two-step process. First\, participants must complete thei
 r registration through this page. After this step\, library staff will fol
 low up to request additional information in order to complete the registra
 tion.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this fo
 rm is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries A
 ct\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used
  for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions a
 bout how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerlin
 e staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toront
 o ON M4W 2G8.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa464b886d8450031156f86
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
