CREATED:20260929
DESCRIPTION:Are you thinking of pursuing your graduate education in Develo
 pment Studies ( https://yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register/JkVwHihoR4-wbOmZGw5
 mnw )? We invite you to attend our program information session! The Gradua
 te Program in Development Studies offers students an intellectually rigoro
 us and relevant interdisciplinary curriculum that is uniquely layered when
  examining theories and practices of development from a critical social sc
 ience perspective. Our research-intensive MA is a uniquely focused\, but f
 lexible graduate program. Through the program\, students pursue a wide ran
 ge of research interests as they relate to the field of development studie
 s in both the Global South and North\, including gender\, education\, heal
 th\, urbanization\, sports\, forced migration\, migrant settlement\, globa
 l environmental crises\, indigeneity\, extractive industries\, precariousn
 ess\, etc. The MA is structured as a five-term program combining coursewor
 k\, fieldwork and internship/placement.\nLearn more about our graduate pro
 grams at futurestudents.yorku.ca/graduate/programs  ( http://futurestudent
 s.yorku.ca/graduate/programs )\nStill have questions? Contact us at fgsa
 pply@yorku.ca ( mailto:fgsapply@yorku.ca ).\nRegistration Required ( https
 ://yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register/JkVwHihoR4-wbOmZGw5mnw ).\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20260929
LOCATION:(URL will be provided in the email confirmation)
ORGANIZER;CN="Faculty of Graduate Studies":MAILTO:fgsinfo@yorku.ca
