DESCRIPTION:Are you thinking of pursuing your graduate education in Transl
 ation ( https://yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register/MnV8h64FQDy1zcVQiYLCmA )? W
 e invite you to attend our program session. Registration is required!\nUnd
 ertake a learning journey in translation that is key to the circulation of
  knowledge\, literature\, and information across the planet. In our multic
 ultural and multilingual academic community — ideally set in Toronto\, t
 he most diverse city in the world — you’ll collaborate with dynamic pr
 ofessors who are experts in many languages and various research areas\, in
 cluding literary translation and reception\, translation theories\, politi
 cal texts and ideology\, crowdsourced translation\, professional deontolog
 y and ethics\, space and mobility\, conflict and intercultural mediation\,
  cultural aspects of translation\, epistemological questions in translatio
 n and interpreting. Whether you want to increase your specialization or pu
 rsue advanced studies in the growing academic field of Translation Studies
 \, you will earn skills that set you apart in the workplace.\nLearn more a
 bout our graduate programs at futurestudents.yorku.ca/graduate/programs  (
  http://futurestudents.yorku.ca/graduate/programs )\nStill have questions?
  Contact us at fgsapply@yorku.ca ( mailto:fgsapply@yorku.ca ).\nRegistra
 tion Required.  ( https://yorku.zoom.us/meeting/register/MnV8h64FQDy1zcVQ
 iYLCmA )\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20260923
LOCATION:(URL will be provided in the email confirmation)
