DESCRIPTION:So\, you’re thinking about grad school! Maybe there were a c
 ouple of courses you just couldn’t get enough of\, or a topic that reall
 y interested you? Perhaps there’s a subject or a specialization in which
  you want to become an expert? Maybe you just want to polish up your criti
 cal and communication skills before conquering the job market? There are m
 any fantastic reasons to consider pursuing a graduate degree… and\, ther
 e can almost as many reasons to feel a little intimidated by the idea. In 
 this session\, FGS Dean Alice MacLachlan will take you through everything 
 you need to know that no one told you\, streamlining and simplifying the i
 dea of grad school and the process of applying. Join us and find out:\nWha
 t are masters and doctorate degrees?\nWhat exactly does a grad student do?
 \nHow do I know which school or degree is right for me?\nHow do I get from
  idea to application?\nWhom do I talk to if I have questions about grad sc
 hool?\nAbout my application?\nHow do I approach a potential program or adv
 isor\nWhat does a grad school application look like?\nWhat will they ask f
 or?\nCan I afford grad school?\nHow much might it cost?\nTips for a strong
  application\nTips for choosing between multiple programs\nHow to manage a
 nxiety and expectations\nThis session is happening as part of Experience G
 rad York. To find other sessions covering graduate admissions at York\, pl
 ease visit https://www.yorku.ca/gradstudies/egy/ ( https://www.yorku.ca/gr
 adstudies/egy/ ).\nIf you have any accessibility requirements for this eve
 nt\, please let us know at fgsapply@yorku.ca ( mailto:fgsapply@yorku.ca ).
 \nRegistration is required ( https://yorku.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_qXd
 AQlSEROSJ5hKfGR3skg ).\n
