DESCRIPTION:This program is part of the Toronto Reference Library's\nEntre
 preneur in Residence\n(EIR) service.\n"Everyone I talked to said they love
 d it" is the most expensive sentence in business. This session teaches you
  how to test an idea properly by identifying fatal assumptions\, designing
  theoretical prototypes\, and engaging customers in conversations that pro
 duce honest answers. We'll cover pre-sales\, waitlists\, and other ways to
  get evidence before you build anything. You'll practice the technique in 
 front of other participants and leave with a better idea of your next step
 s.\nRegistration required\, limited room capacity.\nTo apply for one-on-on
 e consultations with our resident entrepreneur\, Ryan\, please fill out th
 e in-take form available at\ntpl.ca/eir\n. We begin accepting in-take form
 s on September 28\, 2026 until available slots are filled.\nInformation Co
 llection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by th
 e Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\,
  20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and progra
 m registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library 
 handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerlin
 e@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Founders Room\, Ground Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a99ba0b660e510bf441022f
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
