SUMMARY:"Make It Heard": Civic Problem-Solving & Digital Advocacy
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261015T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261015T200000
UID:6a9c750e29a7dd0d674955c6@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Every community has problems. This series gives you the tools 
 to do something about them. Over three sessions you will define a real civ
 ic challenge in your neighbourhood\, design a creative response\, and buil
 d something: a digital campaign\, a poster\, a video pitch\, or even a 3D-
 printed prototype that communicates your idea to the public. Come ready to
  think\, build\, and be heard.\nThis program is part of TPL's Innovator in
  Residence series focused on civic innovation. From October 5 to November 
 28\, join programs\, workshops and one-on-one consultations led by technol
 ogy strategist Ismail Mohamud to learn how technology can help you create 
 positive change in your community. Learn more at\ntpl.ca/iir\n.\nInformati
 on Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected 
 by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20
 (a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and p
 rogram registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the lib
 rary handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nansw
 erline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Digital Innovation Hub
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9c750e29a7dd0d674955c6
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
