SUMMARY:Finding Recovery Through Exercise Skills and Hope (FRESH): Drop In
  Fridays
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261016T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261016T130000
UID:69496312c967cb41207dfccc@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This program helps people stay active\, make friends\, learn n
 ew skills\, and have fun. It involves peer-led group activities including 
 crafts\, games\, walking\, yoga and more. Meet new folks\, build connectio
 ns\, and tell us about programs and services you would like to see in the 
 neighbourhood!\nDrop in\, no registration is required.\nSnacks and refresh
 ments are provided for all participants. Ingredient lists will be availabl
 e at the program.\nThis program is in collaboration with\nGerstein Crisis 
 Centre's F.R.E.S.H. initiative\n.
LOCATION:Parkdale
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69496312c967cb41207dfccc
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults, Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aaad9d33dd190003e726949"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Dear Disabled Black Woman: Film Screening and Q&A
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261016T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261016T130000
UID:6aaad9d33dd190003e726949@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Please join us for a special screening of Dear Disabled Black 
 Woman\, an independently produced film by Ingrid Palmer\, who has partial
  vision and advocates with and for Black and blind communities. The film c
 entres seven Black women with disabilities\, across a range of ages\, cult
 ural backgrounds\, classes\, sexual orientations and disabilities\, as the
 y share their experiences and perspectives on working with a disability in
  Canada. Q&A to follow.\nRegistration recommended. Doors open at 10:30 am.
