SUMMARY:Co-op Information Session
DTSTART:20261016T180000Z
DTEND:20261016T190000Z
DTSTAMP:20261002T131000Z
UID:MEC-1b52316d70bb30edd173db4f2805c856@events.yorku.ca
RECURRENCE-ID:20261016T180000Z
SEQUENCE:2
CATEGORIES:Co-op &amp\; Career Centre,Co-op Information Session,Co-op Mand
 atory Sessions (CCC),Information Sessions (CCC)
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20261002
DESCRIPTION:\nYork University Co-op Information Session (live webinar)\nLo
 cation: Online – Link:  https://yorku.zoom.us/my/askcoop\nDate: Octobe
 r 16\, 2026\nTime: 2:00pm-3:30pm\nThe York University Co-op Program provi
 des students with opportunities for paid\, hands-on learning and valuable 
 industry experience. We encourage you to visit the Co-operative Education 
 website to review program details and confirm that you meet the academic r
 equirements.\nDuring this session\, you will learn about:\n\nThe co-op adv
 antage\nEligibility requirements\nProgram fees\nThe registration process\n
 General Q&A with a Co-op Coordinator\n\nTarget Audience:\nThese sessions a
 re for York University students intending to begin their first co-op work 
 term in Summer 2027. Before registering\, please self-assess your eligibi
 lity for the program ( https://www.yorku.ca/career-ready/work-opportunitie
 s/co-op/eligibility/ ).\n\nLive Session vs. Self-Paced Modules: What’s t
 he Difference?\nBased on student feedback\, we now offer flexible options 
 to complete the required sessions. Each format has unique benefits:\n\nLiv
 e sessions (in-person or webinar): Opportunity to ask questions and inter
 act directly with a Co-op Coordinator.\nSelf-paced eClass modules: Comple
 te the content at a time that is most convenient for you.\n\n\nImportant R
 eminders:\n\nRequired sessions must be completed for your application to b
 e reviewed.\nAlready attended a mandatory session within the last 12 month
 s? You do not need to attend again.\nAlready admitted to Co-op? You are no
 t required to complete the mandatory sessions or re-apply.\nIf you have an
  eligible work term for Summer 2027: Log in to the co-op portal and accept
  the terms and conditions when prompted.\n\nWe look forward to your partic
 ipation!\nHaving trouble logging in? \nPlease make sure you’re using yo
 ur PPY York U login. When you select SSO (Single Sign-On)\, you should be 
 prompted to sign in with your PPY credentials. If you use a different logi
 n\, you may not be able to access the system.\nRegister Here [icon name=
 ”chevron-right” class=”small pl-2″]\n \nAccessibility\nIf you req
 uire accommodations\, please contact askcoop@yorku.ca\, and a member of o
 ur team will follow up with you.\nCode of Conduct\nBefore attending\, plea
 se review the Code of Rights and Responsibilities from the York Universi
 ty Office of Student Community Relations to help ensure a respectful and p
 ositive experience for all participants.\nGuests who exhibit behaviour tha
 t violates this code may be removed from the event. If you experience beha
 viour that does not align with these expectations\, please contact our tea
 m at askcoop@yorku.ca.\n \n
LAST-MODIFIED:20261002
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/co-op-information-session-3/
X-SOURCE:York University
END:VEVENT
