SUMMARY:Orientation Intensive
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261016T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261016T200000
UID:6a9c776329a7dd0d674955dd@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Missed one of our orientation sessions? This single session br
 ings together everything from the first three: an introduction to civic in
 novation and the Civix by Design program\, a walkthrough of Toronto Open D
 ata and public datasets\, and a hands-on tour of the tools we will use. It
  is a fast-paced overview designed to get you fully caught up and ready to
  participate in any session in the series.\nThis program is part of TPL's 
 Innovator in Residence series focused on civic innovation. From October 5 
 to November 28\, join programs\, workshops and one-on-one consultations le
 d by technology strategist Ismail Mohamud to learn how technology can help
  you create positive change in your community. Learn more at\ntpl.ca/iir\n
 .\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form i
 s collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\,
  sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for
  event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about
  how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline st
 aff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON
  M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Small Meeting Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9c776329a7dd0d674955dd
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
