SUMMARY:Wildlife-friendly Fall Gardens
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261017T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261017T150000
UID:6a6a4869f213992f00c7f72b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:At this time of year\, many people admire the fall colours but
  also feel the need to rake and dispose of leaves\, cut dead stems\, and r
 emove fallen branches. But what if this tidying up negatively affects our 
 gardens and pollinators? While we may not see the bees and butterflies dur
 ing the fall and winter\, they are still around!\nIn this presentation\, D
 orte Windmuller\, a Butterflyway Ranger of the David Suzuki Foundation\, w
 ill discuss how to maintain and protect wildlife habitat even throughout t
 he colder months\, and how “leave the leaves” can help nature come bac
 k stronger the next season.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal 
 information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under 
 the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The informa
 tion will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and e
 valuation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be
  directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789
  Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Room B1 (located in the basement)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a6a4869f213992f00c7f72b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Young Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abe8d069d27a000454de05b"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_young_adults
SUMMARY:Human Rights for Everyone! A Discussion of Democracy\, Freedoms\, 
  & Protections in Toronto.
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261017T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261017T160000
UID:6abe8d069d27a000454de05b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Are you interested in learning more about your rights?\nJoin u
 s for an interactive and informative session with the\nCanadian Civil Libe
 rties Education Trust (CCLET).\nWe will discuss the Charter of Rights and 
 Freedoms\, the Ontario Human Rights Code\, and rights and freedoms in Cana
 da – including freedom of expression\, protest rights\, protections agai
 nst discrimination and more!\nLogo for CCLET - Canadian Civil Liberties Ed
 ucation Trust\nToronto's municipal election takes place on October 26\, 20
 26. Check out the\nKnowYourVote.TO\nwebsite and the\nCelebrate Democracy\
 npage to learn more about the upcoming election\, access important voter r
 esources\, and discover more activities and interactive library programs f
 or all ages happening at a branch near you.\nThis initiative is made possi
 ble by donations to the Toronto Public Library Foundation and is generousl
 y supported by the McConnell Foundation
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 101\, first floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abe8d069d27a000454de05b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
