X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a554b12f213992f00c3f847"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Moving Stories: A Movement Class for Older Adults
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261019T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261019T113000
UID:6a554b12f213992f00c3f847@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In this series\, participants will be introduced to the world 
 of art and creative storytelling through movement and music. These activit
 ies have been proven to improve circulation and joint mobility\, promote m
 ental stimulation\, improve posture and coordination\, and build strength 
 and balance. No previous movement experience is required. Each class build
 s upon the previous\, so participants are encouraged to attend each week.\
 nThis program is intended for\nolder adults\n.\nMoving Stories is brought 
 to you by tiger princess dance projects.\nRegistration for this program is
  now closed.\nMoving Stories is generously supported by the Canada Counci
 l for the Arts\, Ontario Arts Council & Toronto Arts Council.\nInformation
  Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by
  the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a
 )\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and pro
 gram registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the libra
 ry handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswer
 line@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Pape/Danforth\, Second floor program room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a554b12f213992f00c3f847
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
