SUMMARY:Lectures & Snacks: Campus Farming for Health and Food Justice
DTSTART:20261019T170000Z
DTEND:20261019T190000Z
DTSTAMP:20260901T131400Z
UID:MEC-6ef43ab936ea0c3ff156b0e099c783ba@events.yorku.ca
RECURRENCE-ID:20261019T170000Z
SEQUENCE:2
CATEGORIES:Advising,Athletics &amp\; Recreation,Colleges,Divisions and Spe
 cial Areas,Faculty of Environmental &amp\; Urban Change,Faculty of Graduat
 e Studies (Programs),Faculty of Health,Faculty of Liberal Arts &amp\; Prof
 essional Studies,Faculty of Science,Glendon,Health Education &amp\; Promot
 ion,Lassonde School of Engineering,Learning Commons,Learning Skills Servic
 es,School of the Arts, Media, Performance &amp\; Design,Schulich School of
  Business,Student Counselling, Health &amp\; Well-being,Student Life,Stude
 nts,the Atkinson Centre for Mature and Part-time Students,The Centre,Well-
 being
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260901
DESCRIPTION:Calling all graduate and mature students – come for the snac
 ks\, stay for the stories!\nLectures & Snacks is your chance to mingle wit
 h fellow York grad and mature students over light refreshments while enjoy
 ing a short\, engaging talk by a student\, faculty or staff member. Think 
 of it as a mini lecture with maximum curiosity…and snacks!\nSession #1: 
 Campus Farming for Health and Food Justice\nSpeaker: Phyllis Novak\, Direc
 tor of Maloca Living Labs – Community and Native Plant Gardens at York U
 niversity\nReady to trade the library for the garden? Tour Maloca Communit
 y Gardens\, York University’s very own campus farm\, and dig into regene
 rative agriculture\, land relationships and community gardening. Discover 
 how growing food on campus connects to sustainability\, climate action\, c
 ommunity health and food justice. This session includes a guided tour\, a 
 short talk and some light earthwork (yes\, you can get your hands a little
  dirty – if you want to!).\nYou’re welcome to drop in\, but if you thi
 nk you’ll be coming\, please register. Registration helps us plan for en
 ough food\, without so much that it goes to waste (because food sustainabi
 lity matters here too!). It also lets us account for allergies and dietary
  preferences\, so everyone can enjoy the snacks safely.\nDate: Monday\, Oc
 tober 19\nTime: 1 – 3PM\nLocation: Maloca Gardens ( https://maps.app.goo
 .gl/iGT6HjAAGxA3qGT69 ) [South west corner of Keele campus]\nCome connect 
 with other curious grad and mature students\, enjoy a snack and leave with
  fresh ideas (and maybe a few new friends).\nRegister for Lectures and Sna
 cks: Campus Farming for Health and Food Justice ( https://forms.students.y
 orku.ca/view.php?id=503705 )\n \n
LAST-MODIFIED:20260901
LOCATION:Maloca Garden\, York University @ 4700 Keele Street\, Toronto ON 
 M3J 1P3
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/lectures-snacks-campus-farming-for-heal
 th-and-food-justice/
X-SOURCE:York University
END:VEVENT
