SUMMARY:Co-op Information Session: In Person
DTSTART:20261019T183000Z
DTEND:20261019T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20261002T132500Z
UID:MEC-3946286620b2e1ed380a77193fb7add7@events.yorku.ca
RECURRENCE-ID:20261019T183000Z
SEQUENCE:4
CATEGORIES:Co-op &amp\; Career Centre,Co-op Information Session,Co-op Mand
 atory Sessions (CCC),Information Sessions (CCC)
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20261002
DESCRIPTION:\nYork University Co-op Information Session \nDate: October 1
 9\, 2026\nTime: 2:30pm-4:00pm\nLocation: Victor Phillip Dahdaleh Building\
 , Room 1012\nThe York University Co-op Program provides students with oppo
 rtunities for paid\, hands-on learning and valuable industry experience. W
 e encourage you to visit the Co-operative Education website to review prog
 ram details and confirm that you meet the academic requirements.\nDuring t
 his session\, you will learn about:\n\nThe co-op advantage\nEligibility re
 quirements\nProgram fees\nThe registration process\nGeneral Q&A with a Co-
 op Coordinator\n\nWho should attend? These sessions are for York Universit
 y students intending to begin their first co-op work term in Summer 2027.
  Before registering\, please self-assess your eligibility for the program
  ( https://www.yorku.ca/career-ready/work-opportunities/co-op/eligibility/
  ).\nLive Session vs. Self-Paced Modules: What’s the Difference?\nBased 
 on student feedback\, we now offer flexible options to complete the requir
 ed sessions. Each format has unique benefits:\n\nLive sessions (in-person 
 or webinar): Opportunity to ask questions and interact directly with a Co
 -op Coordinator.\nSelf-paced eClass modules: Complete the content at a ti
 me that is most convenient for you.\n\nImportant Reminders:\n\nRequired se
 ssions must be completed for your application to be reviewed.\nAlready att
 ended a mandatory session within the last 12 months? You do not need to at
 tend again.\nAlready admitted to Co-op? You are not required to complete t
 he mandatory sessions or re-apply.\nIf you have an eligible work term for 
 Summer 2027: Log in to the co-op portal and accept the terms and condition
 s when prompted.\n\nWe look forward to your participation!\nHaving trouble
  logging in? \nPlease make sure you’re using your PPY York U login. Whe
 n you select SSO (Single Sign-On)\, you should be prompted to sign in with
  your PPY credentials. If you use a different login\, you may not be able 
 to access the system.\nRegister Here [icon name=”chevron-right” class=
 ”small pl-2″]\n \nAccessibility\nIf you require accommodations\, plea
 se contact askcoop@yorku.ca\, and a member of our team will follow up wit
 h you.\nCode of Conduct\nBefore attending\, please review the Code of Rig
 hts and Responsibilities from the York University Office of Student Commu
 nity Relations to help ensure a respectful and positive experience for all
  participants.\nGuests who exhibit behaviour that violates this code may b
 e removed from the event. If you experience behaviour that does not align 
 with these expectations\, please contact our team at askcoop@yorku.ca.\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20261002
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/co-op-information-session-in-person/
X-SOURCE:York University
END:VEVENT
