SUMMARY:The Romance vs Reality of Entrepreneurship
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261020T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261020T200000
UID:6aaad5c6ca248a00291644a4@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:“The only thing that prepares you to run a business is runni
 ng a business.” – Ben Horowitz.\nWhat is an entrepreneur? One of many 
 lessons learned from Jean’s fourteen-year journey as a passionate food e
 ntrepreneur and her ongoing fifteen-year small business coaching practice 
 is that “entrepreneur” is not a job title. Join us for the first sessi
 on of Entrepreneur in Residence (Newcome Focus)\, Jean Chow's\, residency 
 at the Fort York branch!\nThis session will include:\nSelf-assessment – 
 “Should I Be An Entrepreneur?”\nReflection on your current passion lev
 el.\nBalancing the risks associated with entrepreneurial passion.\nCome ea
 rly to network from 6-6:30pm!\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe persona
 l information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library unde
 r the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The infor
 mation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and
  evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can 
 be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 7
 89 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Fort York\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aaad5c6ca248a00291644a4
