 ; Statistics,Graduate Program in Mechanical Engineering,Graduate Program i
 n Music,Graduate Program in Nursing,Graduate Program in Philosophy,Graduat
 e Program in Physics &amp\; Astronomy,Graduate Program in Political Scienc
 e,Graduate Program in Psychology,Graduate Program in Public Policy, Admini
 stration and Law,Graduate Program in Science &amp\; Technology Studies,Gra
 duate Program in Social &amp\; Political Thought,Graduate Program in Socia
 l Anthrolology,Graduate Program in Social Work,Graduate Program in Socio-L
 egal Studies,Graduate Program in Sociology,Graduate Program in Theatre,Gra
 duate Program in Theatre, Dance &amp\; Performance Studies,Graduate Progra
 m in Translation Studies,Graduate Program in Visual Art,LA&amp\;PS Student
 s-Graduate,Markham Campus
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260928
DESCRIPTION:The Faculty of Graduate Studies is hosting a session entitled 
 Dissertation Proposal Essentials. Join us!\nA strong dissertation proposal
  provides the foundation for a successful research project. A crucial acad
 emic milestone\, the proposal is also an opportunity to refine your resear
 ch questions\, establish the significance of your work\, and develop a cle
 ar plan for moving your research forward. This session explores the key el
 ements of an effective dissertation proposal\, including developing a rese
 arch rationale\, articulating your methodology\, organizing your ideas\, a
 nd aligning your goals with disciplinary expectations. Participants will g
 ain practical strategies for preparing a proposal that communicates the va
 lue and direction of their research with clarity and confidence.\nDate: We
 dnesday October 21\, 2026\nTime: 12:00-1:00 p.m. (ET)\nLocation: Virtual W
 orkshop via Zoom Webinar\nRegistration is required: Registration Form ( ht
 tps://yorku.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_-9MpLwhdSn-5qhP94aJRrg )\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20260928
LOCATION:Online Zoom Webinar @ Online Zoom Webinar
ORGANIZER;CN="Faculty of Graduate Studies":MAILTO:fgsinfo@yorku.ca
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/fgs-event-dissertation-proposal-essenti
 als-october-21/
X-SOURCE:York University
END:VEVENT
