X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events": "https://events.yorku.ca/events/recovery-college-yu-balance-week-1-self-care-making-time-for-your-basic-needs/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events
SUMMARY:Recovery College: YU & Balance Week 1 | Self-care: Making time for
  your basic needs
DTSTART:20261021T170000Z
DTEND:20261021T180000Z
DTSTAMP:20260918T175000Z
UID:MEC-71c5ac516da3a947454404f77fbbf58a@events.yorku.ca
RECURRENCE-ID:20261021T170000Z
SEQUENCE:3
CATEGORIES:Academic Advising &amp\; Student Success,Bethune College,Calume
 t College,Colleges,Divisions and Special Areas,Faculties,Faculty of Educat
 ion,Faculty of Health,Faculty of Liberal Arts &amp\; Professional Studies,
 Faculty of Science,Glendon,Health Education &amp\; Promotion,LA&amp\;PS Co
 lleges,LA&amp\;PS Founders College,LA&amp\;PS McLaughlin College,LA&amp\;P
 S New College,LA&amp\;PS Vanier College,Lassonde School of Engineering,Lea
 rning Commons,Learning Skills Services,Markham Campus,Markham Student Acce
 ssibility Services,School of Continuing Studies,School of the Arts, Media,
  Performance &amp\; Design,Stong College,Student Accessibility Services,St
 udent Counselling, Health &amp\; Well-being,Student Leaders at Markham (SL
 AM),Student Life,Students,the Atkinson Centre for Mature and Part-time Stu
 dents,Well-being
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260918
DESCRIPTION:This session will be offered in person at York University’s 
 Markham Campus and is open to students from all York University campuses.\
 nIn this week’s session of YU & Balance\, we will focus on building real
 istic self-care and time management habits that fit into student life.\nSt
 udents will reflect on questions such as:\n\nWhat motivates me to take car
 e of myself?\nWhat tends to get in the way of self-care?\nHow can I make t
 ime for myself when life gets busy?\n\nThrough discussion and reflection\,
  students will explore ways to prioritize their well-being\, build self-ca
 re into their routines and practice affirmations that support confidence a
 nd motivation.\nThis session is part of a 6-week Recovery College series. 
 For each session attended\, participants will receive $5 on their YU-card.
  To receive the gift card\, you must attend the full session (approximatel
 y 45–60 minutes). Unfortunately\, we’re not able to provide gift cards
  for partial attendance. Gift cards will be emailed after the session to t
 he same email address used to register and join the session.\nSpace is lim
 ited\, and registration is offered on a first-come\, first-served basis. I
 f the session is full and you’d like to be added to the waitlist\, pleas
 e email hstacey@yorku.ca. We’ll reach out if a spot becomes available. I
 f you’re registered but can no longer attend\, please let us know as soo
 n as you can so we can offer your spot to another student.\nRegister for S
 elf-care: Making time for your basic needs ( https://forms.students.yorku.
 ca/view.php?id=497738 )\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20261001
LOCATION:Markham Campus (MK2050)
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/recovery-college-yu-balance-week-1-self
 -care-making-time-for-your-basic-needs/
X-SOURCE:York University
END:VEVENT
