SUMMARY:Bridging Minds: Menopause\, Metabolism and Heart Health: What Chan
 ges at Midlife
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261021T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261021T190000
UID:6aaae9c74ea230006f344c45@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:What happens to your heart and metabolism as you move through 
 menopause? As hormone levels change through the transition\, so can the wa
 y your body manages cholesterol\, blood sugar\, fat and other factors that
  influence long-term heart health.\nJoin Dr. Iliana Lega for the next Brid
 ging Minds: Health & Science Conversations webinar to understand these cha
 nges and what you can do to support your health. Building on last month’
 s conversation about menopause and brain health\, this session broadens th
 e picture to explore heart and metabolic health\, practical strategies for
  prevention\, and what current evidence tells us about the role of menopau
 sal hormone therapy.\nWhat to Expect\nWhat changes during menopause:\nUnde
 rstand how the menopause transition can affect cardiovascular risk factors
 \, metabolism\, body composition and weight.\nWhat you can do:\nExplore pr
 actical lifestyle and preventive strategies to support heart and metabolic
  health during midlife.\nThe role of hormone therapy:\nLearn what current 
 evidence tells us about menopausal hormone therapy and cardiovascular and 
 metabolic health.\nAbout the Presenter\nDr. Iliana Lega is a staff endocri
 nologist at Women’s College Hospital\, and a scientist at the Women’s 
 College Hospital Research and Innovation Institute. Dr. Lega’s clinical 
 interests lie in the area of diabetes\, as well as reproductive endocrinol
 ogy\, including Premature Ovarian Insufficiency (POI)\, Turner syndrome\, 
 polyendocrine metabolic ovarian syndrome (PMOS)\, and Menopause.\nAbout th
 e Series\nBridging Minds: Health & Science Conversations is a partnership 
 between the Toronto Public Library and Women’s College Hospital. Through
  monthly discussions led by experts from across different clinical areas a
 nd scientific disciplines\, this series provides attendees with the opport
 unity to engage directly with our topics and speakers and empowers communi
 ties to navigate health and science topics confidently\, inspiring a futur
 e of informed decision-making.\nLearn more:\nhttps://www.womenscollegehosp
 ital.ca/bridging-minds/\nReserve Your Spot Today!\nThis virtual Zoom event
  is free to join but registration is required. Once registered\, you’ll 
 receive an email with the Zoom link.\nWe can’t wait to see you there!
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aaae9c74ea230006f344c45
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
