SUMMARY:Money Matters: Budgeting & Pricing
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261021T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261021T200000
UID:6ab6cc38129d8e0031f5145d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This program is part of the York Woods Library’s\nEntreprene
 ur in Residence\n(EIR) service.\nIn this hands-on session\, participants w
 ork through startup costs\, learn to price with confidence\, and build a s
 imple cash-flow budget. The session covers why personal and business finan
 ces should be kept separate\, the basics of good record-keeping\, and how 
 to build credit and strong banking relationships. Everyone leaves with a b
 udgeting template they can keep using.\nDrop-in\nTo apply for one-on-one c
 onsultations with our resident entrepreneur\, Leo\, please fill out the in
 -take form available at\ntpl.ca/eir\n. We begin accepting in-take forms on
  September 28\, 2026 until available slots are filled.
LOCATION:York Woods\, Enhanced Learning Centre
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab6cc38129d8e0031f5145d
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
