URL:https://tockify.com/torevent/detail/22917/1792620000000
SUMMARY: New Sounds\, New Space Report Launch + Wavelength Documentary Pr
 emiere
DESCRIPTION:Presented with Sonic Boom\n\n\nOctober 21\, 2026\nWavelength 
 @ St. Anne’s\n\n651 Dufferin St.\n\n6PM\n\nFree - RSVP at http://bit.ly/N
 SNSwl\n\n\nYou are invited to join Wavelength for an evening of original 
 content! Local music lovers will enjoy this free presentation\, panel\, a
 nd screening plus a networking session soundtracked by DJ Uncle Chayne.\n
 \n\nBe the first to view Wavelength: 25 Years of Music & Community\, a sh
 ort documentary written and directed by Ian Daffern (Idfactory) telling t
 he story of Toronto’s unique artist-run concert series and non-profit org
 anization. A who’s who of Canadian music\, this project was scored and mi
 xed by Justin Small (Do Make Say Think\, BODY///GRAVE) and music supervis
 ed by Babs V. Westerholm (Cue Queens) and features interviews with Meliss
 a Auf der Maur (Hole\, Smashing Pumpkins)\, Emilie Hanskamp\, pHoenix Pag
 liacci\, Charles Spearin (Broken Social Scene\, Do Make Say Think)\, and 
 Wavelength’s Jonathan Bunce (AKA Jonny Dovercourt). Additional music by B
 urs\, Luge\, MOONBEAN\, Orbital Ensemble\, Paul Chin\, Pony Da Look\, Ric
 h Aucoin\, Sook-Yin Lee and more.\n\n\nA follow up to 2023’s acclaimed Re
 imagining Music Venues Study\, the launch of the “New Sounds\, New Space”
  report explores different pathways for establishing community hubs for T
 oronto’s grassroots music community. With positive case studies on Hugh’s
  Room Live\, It’s Ok* Studios\, Small World Music and Primal Note Studios
 \, the report shines light on Toronto’s post-COVID music venue landscape 
 while pointing the way forward for imaginative new spaces. Funded by Cana
 da Council for the Arts “Seed” grant!\n\n\nJoin in on the conversation th
 at shapes Toronto’s music culture from the ground up.\n\n\nPoster by Dere
 k Ma\n\n\nSupported by:\n\n\nOntario Creates\n\nOntario Arts Council\n\nT
 oronto Arts Council\n\nThe Canada Council for the Arts\n\nDept of Canadia
 n Heritage\n\nSOCAN Foundation\n\nDICE\n\nGreat Lakes Brewing\n\nAdamson\
 n\nYamaha Canada\n\n
CATEGORIES:Film,St.-Anne's-Parish-Hall
X-TKF-FEATURED-IMAGE:https://d3flpus5evl89n.cloudfront.net/6755f3e6a02aaf
 1c2599e757/6ab434e0cd7aa68c2cc2fa95/scaled_1024.jpg
X-TKF-CUSTOM-PREVIEW:Presented with Sonic Boom October 21\, 2026 Waveleng
 th @ St. Anne’s 651 Dufferin St. 6PM Free - RSVP at http://bit.ly/NSNSwl 
 You are invited to join...
X-TKF-PROMOTION-BUTTON;label=RSVP;skip_details=false:bit.ly/NSNSwl
LOCATION:St. Anne's Parish Hall\,651 Dufferin St\, Toronto\, ON M6K 2B2\,
