DESCRIPTION:Immigration posed a difficult question for interwar Canadian
  socialists. One the one hand\, they promoted a universalist vision of a C
 ooperative Commonwealth\; on the other\, they wished to protect Canadian w
 orkers from foreign competition. This lecture explores how social democrat
 s like J.S. Woodsworth\, Agnes Macphail and A.A. Heaps navigated these tu
 rbulent waters.\nSpeaker: Edward Dunsworth\nRegister (In-Person)\nRegister
  (Online)\n
