SUMMARY:What is Artificial Intelligence?
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261022T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261022T153000
UID:6aac271d129d8e0031f301ac@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:AI technologies have become increasingly prevalent in many asp
 ects of modern life\, including healthcare\, finance\, transportation\, a
 nd entertainment. Some examples of AI applications include virtual assist
 ants like Siri and Alexa\, self-driving cars\, fraud detection systems\, 
 and personalized recommendations in online shopping. Come join this begin
 ner in person class to learn what AI is\, how it learns and predicts outc
 omes\, considerations when using GenAI applications\, and how the Intern
 et of Things (IOT) applies to AI.\nIn this class we will:\nLearn what is A
 rtificial Intelligence and how it interacts in our day to day activities.
 \nGain an understanding of how Artificial Intelligence learns and predict
 s outcomes.\nLearn the importance of how data is integral to how Artifici
 al Intelligence systems are built.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe pe
 rsonal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library
  under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The 
 information will only be used for event and program registration\, deliver
 y and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information
  can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-598
 1\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Deer Park\, Main Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aac271d129d8e0031f301ac
