SUMMARY:Co-op Information Session
DTSTART:20261022T170000Z
DTEND:20261022T183000Z
DTSTAMP:20261001T202800Z
UID:MEC-ce916a6c3a313e568546f66654ee5ee1@events.yorku.ca
RECURRENCE-ID:20261022T170000Z
SEQUENCE:3
CATEGORIES:Co-op &amp\; Career Centre,Co-op Information Session,Co-op Mand
 atory Sessions (CCC),Information Sessions (CCC)
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20261001
DESCRIPTION:\nYork U Co-op Information Session (live webinar)\nLocation: 
 Online – Link:  https://yorku.zoom.us/my/askcoop\nDate: October 22\, 20
 26\nTime: 2:00pm-3:30pm\nThe York University Co-op Program provides stude
 nts with opportunities for paid\, hands-on learning and valuable industry 
 experience. We encourage you to visit the Co-operative Education website t
 o review program details and confirm that you meet the academic requiremen
 ts.\nDuring this session\, you will learn about:\n\nThe co-op advantage\nE
 ligibility requirements\nProgram fees\nThe registration process\nGeneral Q
 &A with a Co-op Coordinator\n\nTarget Audience:\nThese sessions are for Yo
 rk University students intending to begin their first co-op work term in S
 ummer 2027. Before registering\, please self-assess your eligibility for 
 the program ( https://www.yorku.ca/career-ready/work-opportunities/co-op/e
 ligibility/ ).\nLive Session vs. Self-Paced Modules: What’s the Differen
 ce?\nBased on student feedback\, we now offer flexible options to complete
  the required sessions. Each format has unique benefits:\n\nLive sessions 
 (in-person or webinar): Opportunity to ask questions and interact directl
 y with a Co-op Coordinator.\nSelf-paced eClass modules: Complete the cont
 ent at a time that is most convenient for you.\n\nImportant Reminders:\n\n
 Required sessions must be completed for your application to be reviewed.\n
 Already attended a mandatory session within the last 12 months? You do not
  need to attend again.\nAlready admitted to Co-op? You are not required to
  complete the mandatory sessions or re-apply.\n\nIf you have an eligible w
 ork term for Summer 2027: Log in to the co-op portal and accept the terms 
 and conditions when prompted.\n\n\n\nWe look forward to your participation
 !\nRegister Here [icon name=”chevron-right” class=”small pl-2″]\nA
 ccessibility\nIf you require accommodations\, please contact askcoop@york
 u.ca\, and a member of our team will follow up with you.\nCode of Conduct\
 nBefore attending\, please review the Code of Rights and Responsibilities
  from the York University Office of Student Community Relations to help e
 nsure a respectful and positive experience for all participants.\nGuests w
 ho exhibit behaviour that violates this code may be removed from the event
 . If you experience behaviour that does not align with these expectations\
 , please contact our team at askcoop@yorku.ca.\nHaving trouble logging in
 ? \nPlease make sure you’re using your PPY York U login. When you selec
 t SSO (Single Sign-On)\, you should be prompted to sign in with your PPY c
 redentials. If you use a different login\, you may not be able to access t
 he system.\nRegister here:\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20261002
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/co-op-information-session-2/
X-SOURCE:York University
END:VEVENT
