SUMMARY:Music From the Golden Age of Scottish Fiddle Music
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261022T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261022T193000
UID:6aaebf27d6577100383d8cc7@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Alana & Leigh Cline will perform on fiddle and guitar Scottish
  fiddle tunes from the late 1700s and early 1800s. Fiddle music of the tim
 e period will be discussed. The performance will also include some tunes t
 hat have connections to poet Robert Burns.\nSpace/seating is limited. Plea
 se arrive early to secure a spot.
LOCATION:Pape/Danforth\, Urban Living Room - first floor
