BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events": "https://events.yorku.ca/events/waste-audit-training-course/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events
SUMMARY:Waste Audit Training Course
DTSTART:20261023T123000Z
DTEND:20261023T223000Z
DTSTAMP:20261002T145100Z
UID:MEC-d4ce8d58dbccac2aec2197cb4ddafa01@events.yorku.ca
RECURRENCE-ID:20261023T123000Z
SEQUENCE:2
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/1
 0/Waste-Audit-Course-Poster_York.png
CATEGORIES:Co-op &amp\; Career Centre,Colleges,Divisions and Special Areas
 ,Event Planners Network,Faculties,Faculty of Environmental &amp\; Urban Ch
 ange,Faculty of Science,FSc Division of Natural Science,FSc Science, Techn
 ology &amp\; Society,Future Students,Graduate Program in Environmental Stu
 dies,Graduate Program in Science &amp\; Technology Studies,ORUs,Research &
 amp\; Innovation,Special Themes,Students,Sustainability,the Atkinson Centr
 e for Mature and Part-time Students,Workshops &amp\; Webinars (CCC),Y-EMER
 GE,YFile newsletter
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20261002
DESCRIPTION:The contemporary discourse around environmental sustainability
  is shifting from linear extraction models to a Circular Economy. With glo
 bal waste expected to rise sharply by 2050\, managing material flows is es
 sential for resource conservation and climate mitigation. Stricter regulat
 ions are driving this change\, including Extended Producer Responsibility 
 (EPR) frameworks and Environmental\, Social\, and Governance (ESG) mandate
 s. Waste is no longer just an operational byproduct. It is a measurable so
 urce of Scope 3 greenhouse gas emissions and a financial risk for organiza
 tions that fail to adapt. Many institutions have set “Net-Zero” target
 s\, but they often lack the methods to measure their output accurately. Th
 is course fills that gap by teaching participants to quantify and characte
 rize waste streams. The curriculum relies on data-driven auditing rather t
 han estimates or guesswork. This approach gives participants the technical
  skills to spot inefficiencies\, optimize procurement\, ensure compliance\
 , and reduce reliance on landfills.\nA microcredit certificate will be iss
 ued to all participants from CIFAL York-UNITAR.\nInstructor: Dr. Calvin La
 khan ( https://www.linkedin.com/in/calvin-lakhan-ph-d-56329224/ )\, Direct
 or\, Circular Innovation Hub\, York University\nMore Information ( https:/
 /www.yorku.ca/cifal/waste-audit/ )\nRegistration link ( https://www.eventb
 rite.com/e/2002212106308?aff=oddtdtcreator )\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20261002
LOCATION:Room N004 Schulich School of Business Building (Basement Floor)
ORGANIZER;CN="CIFAL York":MAILTO:cifalpresident@yorku.ca
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/waste-audit-training-course/
X-SOURCE:York University
END:VEVENT
