SEQUENCE:12
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Graduate Studies,Graduate Program in Communication a
 nd Culture,Graduate Program in Development Studies,Graduate Program in Dis
 aster &amp\; Emergency Management,Graduate Program in Economics,Graduate P
 rogram in English,Graduate Program in Financial Accountability,Graduate Pr
 ogram in Gender, Feminist and Women's Studies,Graduate Program in History,
 Graduate Program in Human Resources Management,Graduate Program in Humanit
 ies,Graduate Program in Information Systems &amp\; Technology,Graduate Pro
 gram in Interdisciplinary Studies,Graduate Program in Linguistics &amp\; A
 pplied Linguistics,Graduate Program in Management Practice,Graduate Progra
 m in Philosophy,Graduate Program in Political Science,Graduate Program in 
 Public Policy, Administration and Law,Graduate Program in Science &amp\; T
 echnology Studies,Graduate Program in Social &amp\; Political Thought,Grad
 uate Program in Social Anthrolology,Graduate Program in Social Work,Gradua
 te Program in Socio-Legal Studies,Graduate Program in Sociology,LA&amp\;PS
  Colleges,LA&amp\;PS New College
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260924
DESCRIPTION:The Writing Centre and New College are running a 2-hour Propos
 al Writing workshop designed to help clarify the process and help you make
  progress. Writing proposals at the Graduate-Level carries with it a whole
  array of expectations that are often unclear. This workshop is designed t
 o clarify some of what those expectations entail\, and to help you develop
  strategies to better navigate the demands of proposal writing to set you 
 up well for your longer-form projects. A one-to-one appointment with the W
 riting Centre graduate writing specialist (at a time of your choosing) is 
 included so that you’ll also receive targeted and detailed feedback on y
 our draft.\nRegistration is required.  Register Now!\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20260925
LOCATION:002 Atkinson
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
