SUMMARY:Design Jam: Kids
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261024T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261024T140000
UID:6abec8e3c6cddb00459554b0@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:A fast-paced\, fun session where young creators tackle a real 
 community challenge through brainstorming\, sketching\, and creative think
 ing. There are no wrong answers\, just ideas\, energy\, and collaboration.
  If time allows\, you might even start building a simple version of your s
 olution.\nThis program is part of TPL's Innovator in Residence series focu
 sed on civic innovation. From October 5 to November 28\, join programs\, w
 orkshops and one-on-one consultations led by technology strategist Ismail 
 Mohamud to learn how technology can help you create positive change in you
 r community. Learn more at\ntpl.ca/iir\n.\nInformation Collection Notice:\
 nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public 
 Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d
 ). The information will only be used for event and program registration\, 
 delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your info
 rmation can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-
 397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Second Floor\, Digital Innovation Hub
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abec8e3c6cddb00459554b0
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
