X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_toronto_heavy_boardgamers
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Toronto Heavy Boardgamers
UID:event_316231810@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261003T050451Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261025T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261025T180000
SUMMARY:Toronto East Weekend Gaming @ Face-to-Face Games
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Heavy Boardgamers\nWelcome to the Sunday meetup for To
 ronto Heavy Boardgamers @ Face-to-Face Games!\n\nThe purpose of this event
  is to meet up to play heavier / longer board games\, and have fun while d
 oing it! We will start off small and if there is sufficient interest we wi
 ll add capacity for future events.\n\n**Scheduling details:**\n\n\\- If yo
 u have a specific game that you would like to post for\\\, feel free to do
  so in comments\\. In your post\\\, include the name of the game\\\, numbe
 r of players needed for the game\\\, whether you are offering a teach or n
 ot\\\, and the start time \\(please try to start before noon if possible\\
 )\\.\n\n\\- If you would like to join a specific game that has already bee
 n posted\\\, feel free to comment on it confirming your participation\\. M
 ake sure you have noted the details posted by the host\\.\n\n\\- You are o
 f course also welcome to organize / join games onsite on the day itself\\\
 , assuming sufficient players / tables are available\n\n**Rules around COV
 ID:**\n\n\\- Given this is a public event\\\, we respectfully ask that onl
 y i\\) fully vaccinated individuals\\\, and ii\\) those not exhibiting any
  COVID symptoms\\\, participate\\. This requirement may change in the futu
 re based on provincial guidelines and group requirements\n\n**Admission Fe
 e:**\n\n\\- There are no table fees for this event
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/toronto-heavy-boardgamers/events/3162
 31810/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260822T205549Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260822T205549Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Batashoemuseum": "https://batashoemuseum.ca/event/fall-exhibition-kickoff/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:batashoemuseum
X-SOURCE:Bata Shoe Museum
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261025T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261025T160000
DTSTAMP:20260915T213054Z
CREATED:20260826T163152Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260915T213054Z
UID:17022-1792929600-1792944000@batashoemuseum.ca
SUMMARY:Fall Exhibition Kickoff
DESCRIPTION:Date: Sunday\, October 25\, 2026\nTime: 12:00 pm to 4:00 pm\nLocation: Bata Shoe Museum\nTickets: Included with General Admission \nCelebrate the opening of our fall exhibition\, Brilliant: The Art of Beaded Footwear around the World — an exhibition spanning 400 years of history and five corners of the globe\, from Indigenous North America and West Africa to South and Southeast Asia\, Europe\, and Western fashion. \nJoin us for a full afternoon of family-friendly fun\, with guided tours through over 85 extraordinary objects\, hands-on beading crafts for all ages\, and conversations with artists who have dedicated their practice to this meticulous\, centuries-old art form. Discover how a single bead — fragile\, painstaking\, and deeply symbolic — has adorned footwear across cultures\, and explore what the future of this remarkable craft might look like. \nA perfect day out for the whole family. Come curious\, leave inspired!  \nRSVP  \nEvent Schedule\nGuided Exhibition Tours\n12:30 pm\, 1:30 pm\, 2:30 pm\, 3:30 pm\nEach tour is approximately 30 minutes. \nSelf-Guided Crafts\n12:00 pm – 4:00 pm\nDrop-in activities for families and children of all ages. \nBeads Presentation\n1:00 pm\nGuided by local artist Marissa Magneson. \nSelf-guided crafts will be available throughout the day. Children must be accompanied by an adult. Activities and giveaways are available while supplies last. Schedule subject to change. \nTo ensure a safe and enjoyable experience for all visitors\, please review our Terms & Conditions to learn more about Visitor & Accessibility Services\, Ticketing\, Returns & Exchanges\, Privacy & Media\, and more.
URL:https://batashoemuseum.ca/event/fall-exhibition-kickoff/
CATEGORIES:Drop In Activity,Special Event
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://batashoemuseum.ca/wp-content/uploads/Beads_Community_Day_1.jpg
END:VEVENT
