CATEGORIES:Academic Advising &amp\; Student Success,Colleges,Faculty of Ed
 ucation,Faculty of Environmental &amp\; Urban Change,Faculty of Graduate S
 tudies,Faculty of Health,Faculty of Liberal Arts &amp\; Professional Studi
 es,Faculty of Science,LA&amp\;PS Founders College,LA&amp\;PS IEP Bridging 
 Program,LA&amp\;PS McLaughlin College,LA&amp\;PS New College,LA&amp\;PS Va
 nier College,Lassonde School of Engineering,School of Continuing Studies,S
 chool of the Arts, Media, Performance &amp\; Design,the Atkinson Centre fo
 r Mature and Part-time Students
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260929
DESCRIPTION:This workshop focuses on using Microsoft Copilot\, when permit
 ted\, as a thinking and planning aid to support academic work without repl
 acing your own ideas or writing. Participants will learn how to use Copilo
 t in ways that align with York University’s academic integrity expectati
 ons\, including the Senate Policy on Academic Conduct\, through practical 
 strategies for clarifying tasks\, planning next steps\, and reviewing thei
 r own work. \nDate: Tuesday October 27th\, 2026 \nTime: 12:00pm- 1:00pm
  \nLocation: Zoom  \nRegister here: https://yorku.zoom.us/meeting/regis
 ter/K80TfMmQQMeZN_jtTQCb-w  \n
