SUMMARY:The Three “Know’s for Success as an Entrepreneur
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261027T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261027T200000
UID:6aaad5e3ab7a8e0037c24145@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In this highly interactive workshop with Entrepreneur in Resid
 ence (Newcomer Focus)\, Jean Chow\, we’ll explore how well you know your
 self\, know your reason why you want to own a business\, and will your cus
 tomers need and want to buy what you are offering. What are the key traits
  of an entrepreneur? Is this an opportunity worth pursuing\, a T.R.U.E. (T
 estable\, Real. Unique\, Essential) value proposition? Who are your custom
 ers?\nThis session will include:\nKnow your dominant dimension as an entre
 preneur – “heart\, smarts\, guts\, or luck”.\nPinpoint your “why
 ” with your T.R.U.E. value proposition and articulate the problem you ar
 e solving. Is it an opportunity worth pursuing?\nCreate a buyer persona/id
 eal customer profile (ICP) to demonstrate how well you know your target au
 dience.\nCome early to network from 6-6:30pm!\nInformation Collection Noti
 ce:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Pub
 lic Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 
 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registratio
 n\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your 
 information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 
 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Fort York\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aaad5e3ab7a8e0037c24145
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
