SUMMARY:How to disassemble a desktop computer! Workshop for teens
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261027T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261027T200000
UID:6a91e758b204780029964c8b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Have you ever wondered what's going on inside a computer? Ever
  wanted to see a computer taken apart? This workshop is your chance! Durin
 g this workshop\, we'll go over what's inside a computer\, how to properly
  open a desktop\, and safety guidelines to follow when it comes to working
  with electronics. Q&A included.\nAll teens are welcome!\nThis presentatio
 n is hosted by Free Geek Toronto\, a non-profit organization that refurbi
 shes discarded computers and makes them useful tools again for people who 
 need them.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on th
 is form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Librar
 ies Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be
  used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questi
 ons about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answ
 erline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, T
 oronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Morningside\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a91e758b204780029964c8b
