BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events": "https://events.yorku.ca/events/euc-co-op-information-session/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events
SUMMARY:EUC Co-op Information Session
DTSTART:20261028T173000Z
DTEND:20261028T183000Z
DTSTAMP:20261002T133200Z
UID:MEC-cc0843a977aad2421486ae32ccc2c018@events.yorku.ca
RECURRENCE-ID:20261028T173000Z
SEQUENCE:2
CATEGORIES:Co-op &amp\; Career Centre,Co-op Information Session,Co-op Mand
 atory Sessions (CCC),Faculty of Environmental &amp\; Urban Change,Informat
 ion Sessions (CCC)
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20261002
DESCRIPTION:\nCo-op is available for students in Environmental Arts & Just
 ice\, Sustainable Environmental Management\, Cities\, Regions & Planning\,
  and Global Geography.\nThe York University Co-op Program provides student
 s with an opportunity for paid\, hands-on learning and industry experience
 .\nCo-op Information Session for Environmental & Urban Change (EUC) studen
 ts\nDate: October 28\, 2026\nTime: 1:30 pm-2:30 pm\nJoin us to learn about
 :\n\nCo-op and Internship Advantage\nEligibility Requirements\nFees\nRegis
 tration Process\nGeneral Q & A\n\nWhat’s the difference between attendin
 g a live session or webinar and engaging in  the self-paced/asynchronous 
 modules on the Co-op Preparatory Course (eClass)? \n\nWe value students
 ’ feedback and based on past feedback\, students asked for flexible ways
  to complete the required sessions. There are benefits to each modality. T
 he benefit of attending the live session is that you will have a Q& A sess
 ion with a Co-op Coordinator. The benefit of completing the sessions throu
 gh eClass via learning modules is that you can complete these at a time th
 at is more convenient for you!\n\nIMPORTANT REMINDERS: \n\nAlready admitt
 ed to Co-op? You are not required to complete the mandatory sessions agai
 n. You do not need to re-apply to the program to state your interest. If y
 ou have an eligible work term for Fall 2027\, simply log-in to the portal
  and accept the terms and conditions.\n\nWe are looking forward to your pa
 rticipation!\nRegister Here [icon name=”chevron-right” class=”small 
 pl-2″]\nACCESSIBILITY: Should you require accommodations\, please contac
 t us at askcoop@yorku.ca and a member of our team will connect with you r
 egarding your request.\nCODE OF CONDUCT\nPrior to the event\, we kindly as
 k you to review the Code of Rights and Responsibilities from the York Univ
 ersity Office of Student Community Relations\, so that we can ensure an en
 joyable experience for everyone in our community. Please note\, guests who
  exhibit behaviours that violate this code will be exited from the event b
 y the hosts. If you face behaviours that violate this code\, please connec
 t with our team at askcoop@yorku.ca.\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20261002
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/euc-co-op-information-session/
X-SOURCE:York University
