SUMMARY:Digital Privacy 201
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261029T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261029T153000
UID:6ab7d77608693b0f7374c2d2@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This is the second session in the Digital Privacy 101 series a
 nd is intended for participants who have completed Part 1. Learn practical
  strategies to keep your personal information safe online\, including esse
 ntial digital privacy habits\, creating and managing strong passwords\, an
 d recognizing common online threats such as phishing\, malware\, and hacki
 ng. Gain the knowledge and confidence to make safer choices online.\nRegis
 tration begins Oct 15\nPrerequisites:\nSome computer experience is require
 d\; the ability to navigate app menus\, browsers\, and desktop computing f
 eatures is desirable.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal inform
 ation on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Pu
 blic Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information w
 ill only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluat
 ion. Questions about how the library handles your information can be direc
 ted to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge
  Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Eglinton Square\, Meeting Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab7d77608693b0f7374c2d2
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
