BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events": "https://events.yorku.ca/events/recovery-college-yu-balance-week-2-finding-self-compassion-and-dealing-with-growing-pains/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events
SUMMARY:Recovery College: YU & Balance Week 2 | Finding self-compassion an
 d dealing with growing pains
DTSTART:20261029T160000Z
DTEND:20261029T170000Z
DTSTAMP:20260918T175500Z
UID:MEC-fa1dcf25e93feabd8335f5d20bff7172@events.yorku.ca
RECURRENCE-ID:20261029T160000Z
SEQUENCE:3
CATEGORIES:Academic Advising &amp\; Student Success,Advising,Bethune Colle
 ge,Calumet College,Colleges,Faculties,Faculty of Health,Faculty of Liberal
  Arts &amp\; Professional Studies,Faculty of Science,Glendon,Health Educat
 ion &amp\; Promotion,LA&amp\;PS Colleges,LA&amp\;PS Founders College,LA&am
 p\;PS McLaughlin College,LA&amp\;PS New College,LA&amp\;PS Vanier College,
 Lassonde School of Engineering,Learning Commons,Learning Skills Services,M
 arkham Campus,Markham Student Accessibility Services,School of Continuing 
 Studies,School of the Arts, Media, Performance &amp\; Design,Stong College
 ,Student Accessibility Services,Student Counselling, Health &amp\; Well-be
 ing,Student Leaders at Markham (SLAM),Student Life,Students,the Atkinson C
 entre for Mature and Part-time Students,Well-being
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260918
DESCRIPTION:This session will be offered in person at York University’s 
 Markham Campus and is open to students from all York University campuses.\
 nGrowth does not always mean having everything figured out.\nThis week’s
  session of YU & Balance is about giving yourself room to explore your int
 erests\, set goals that feel meaningful and recognize that responsibilitie
 s and personal ambitions can exist together. Students will be able to take
  a closer look at where they are now and where they would like to go\, whi
 le also considering the role self-compassion plays when plans change\, mis
 takes happen or progress feels slow. What would you pursue if you gave you
 rself permission to try? And what would it look like to support yourself a
 long the way instead of criticizing every setback?\nThis session is part o
 f a 6-week Recovery College series. For each session attended\, participan
 ts will receive $5 on their YU-card. To receive the gift card\, you must a
 ttend the full session (approximately 45–60 minutes). Unfortunately\, we
 ’re not able to provide gift cards for partial attendance. Gift cards wi
 ll be emailed after the session to the same email address used to register
  and join the session.\nSpace is limited\, and registration is offered on 
 a first-come\, first-served basis. If the session is full and you’d like
  to be added to the waitlist\, please email hstacey@yorku.ca ( mailto:hsta
 cey@yorku.ca ). We’ll reach out if a spot becomes available. If you’re
  registered but can no longer attend\, please let us know as soon as you c
 an so we can offer your spot to another student.\nRegister for Finding sel
 f-compassion and dealing with growing pains ( https://forms.students.yorku
 .ca/view.php?id=498420 )\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20261001
LOCATION:Markham Campus (MK2050)
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/recovery-college-yu-balance-week-2-find
 ing-self-compassion-and-dealing-with-growing-pains/
X-SOURCE:York University
END:VEVENT
