BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Teens": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9b4e3d3b6c71003e5de731"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_teens
SUMMARY:AI for School: Responsible Success for Teens
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261029T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261029T180000
UID:6a9b4e3d3b6c71003e5de731@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:AI can help with schoolwork. So why does it feel like walking 
 a tightrope? How do you use it for learning without fooling yourself?\nIn 
 this youth-focused class\, you'll learn to use AI as a tutor\, quiz partne
 r\, and explainer\, not an answer machine. You'll practice the tutor loop 
 using provided examples: starting with what your interests are\, what you 
 want to learn\, how you like to learn\, and what you already understand. W
 e'll also cover academic policies around AI and when AI is the wrong tool 
 entirely.\nPrerequisites: Mouse\, keyboarding and internet skills. Compu
 ters are provided. No coding experience required.\nRegistration is requir
 ed and will start September 9\, 2026 at 9:00 AM.\nNote: Your spot will not
  be guaranteed after 5 minutes of the start of the program.\nAfter this ti
 me\, remaining seats will be filled on a first come\, first serve basis un
 til capacity is reached. If you wish to save your work from this hands-on
  program\, please bring your own USB stick.\nAbout the AI Tools Used in Th
 is Program\nThis program includes activities that use agentic AI tools (li
 sted below) on library laptops.\nYou do not need to create your own accoun
 t for this program.\nParticipants are encouraged to follow the Resident’
 s guidance throughout sessions\, which include best practices on using AI.
 \nWe encourage you to review the privacy statements of each tool prior to 
 attending this program:\nClaude Code\nLearn more about the tool\nReview pr
 ivacy policy\nGoogle Antigravity\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privac
 y policy\nGoogle AI Studio\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy poli
 cy\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form 
 is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\
 , sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used fo
 r event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions abou
 t how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline s
 taff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto O
 N M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd Floor eLearning Lab
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9b4e3d3b6c71003e5de731
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
