SUMMARY:Youth Hub: Boba Drink Making with Chef Yuminko
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261029T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261029T170000
UID:6a989bf04cb69d003e25577a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Chef Yumiko leads a hands-on workshop to make the popular Asia
 n beverage\, Brown Sugar Milk with Boba. Participants will learn to prepar
 e and use the classic ingredients including milk\, molasses and tapioca pe
 arls to make this visually pleasing and sweet drink. Chef Yumiko will also
  provide a brief history of Boba and why it's so popular globally.\nFood a
 llergy notice:\nPlease be aware that food will be used in this program. Ce
 rtain food ingredients may cause allergic reactions in some people.\nThis 
 is a Youth Hub program for teens.\nRegistration Required. No Waitlist. Spo
 ts held for five minutes only.\nThis program is part of Youth Hub service.
  Youth Hubs are a welcoming place for teens after school and in the summer
 \, where helpful staff are always available. Free\, nutritious snacks are
  offered daily. Drop by a branch with a\nYouth Hub\nor call the branch to
  find out more.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information 
 on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public L
 ibraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will on
 ly be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Q
 uestions about how the library handles your information can be directed to
  Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Stree
 t\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Eatonville\, Program Rm.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a989bf04cb69d003e25577a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
