SUMMARY:Book Launch: “Austerity & Resistance: The Ontario Days of Action
 \, 1995-1998”
DTSTART:20261029T200000Z
DTEND:20261029T220000Z
DTSTAMP:20261002T145100Z
UID:MEC-00fae5fc28cb7bd60be9ab6609b9bbf7@events.yorku.ca
RECURRENCE-ID:20261029T200000Z
SEQUENCE:2
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/
 09/YFile_Banner-scaled.jpg
CATEGORIES:LA&amp\;PS Department of Politics,LA&amp\;PS Open to the Public
 ,Research &amp\; Innovation,YFile newsletter
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20261002
DESCRIPTION:[HYBRID EVENT – Author in attendance (in-person)!]\nJoin us 
 online and in-person for the launch of Paul Kellogg’s new book Austerity
  and Resistance: The Ontario Days of Action\, 1995–1998. Published 30 ye
 ars after the Toronto general strike of October 1996\, Austerity and Resis
 tance aims to tell its story of the social movement and lessons that we ca
 n carry forward today.\nThe launch event will feature a moderated panel di
 scussion and author remarks. Light refreshments will be served.\n[Register
  for the event here ( https://forms.gle/M1KvGbqyDoHtTnDV8 )]\n—-\nPaneli
 sts: \n\nJudy Rebick\, author of Heroes in My Head (House of Anansi Press\
 , 2018)\nEsther Reiter\, author of A Future Without Hate or Need (Between 
 the Lines\, 2016)\nHerman Rosenfeld\, retired national staff\, Canadian Au
 to Workers (Unifor)\n\nPanel Moderator: Phil Henderson\, Banting Postdocto
 ral Fellow at the GLRC\nFor questions\, email glrc@yorku.ca.\nEvent coordi
 nated by the Global Labour Research Centre (GLRC) at York University\, and
  co-sponsored by Society for Socialist Studies and the Department of Polit
 ics\, Faculty of Liberal Arts & Professional Studies at York University.\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20261002
LOCATION:4700 Keele St\, Ian MacDonald Blvd\, North York\, ON M3J 1P3
ORGANIZER;CN="Global Labour Research Centre":MAILTO:glrc@yorku.ca
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/book-launch-austerity-resistance-the-on
 tario-days-of-action-1995-1998/
X-SOURCE:York University
END:VEVENT
