BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a7a0b7acca66c2f00a9979b"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aaec6b7129d8e0031f38f82"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Finding Recovery Through Exercise Skills and Hope (FRESH)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261104T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261104T150000
UID:6aaec6b7129d8e0031f38f82@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This\n program helps people stay active\, make friends\, learn
  new skills\, and \nhave fun. It involves peer-led group activities which 
 can include crafts\, games\,\n walking\, yoga\, and more. Meet new folks\
 , build social connections\, and tell us\n about programs and services you
  would like to see in the neighbourhood!\nFor our upcoming sessions\, we w
 ill be screening the following films in Program Room A:\nOctober 7:\nSingi
 n' in the Rain\nOctober 14:\nCoco\nOctober 21:\nThe Social Network\nOctobe
 r 28:\nThe King's Speech\nNovember 4:\nEternal Sunshine of the Spotless Mi
 nd\nNovember 11:\nLady Bird\nNovember 18:\nJuno\nNovember 25:\nThe Breakfa
 st Club\nDecember 2:\nMy Cousin Vinny\nDecember 9:\nSecondhand Lions\nDece
 mber 16:\nBlack Swan\nDecember 23:\nScrooged\nDecember 30:\nThe Pursuit of
  Happyness\nDrop in. No registration required.\nSnacks and refreshments ar
 e provided for all participants. Ingredient lists will be available at th
 e program.\nThis program is in collaboration with\nGerstein Crisis Centre'
 s F.R.E.S.H. initiative\n.
LOCATION:Maria A. Shchuka\, Meeting Room A
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aaec6b7129d8e0031f38f82
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab6913c3dd190003e7487d2"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Be Ready\, Toronto! Emergency Preparedness Workshop for Individual
 s
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261104T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261104T140000
UID:6ab6913c3dd190003e7487d2@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Emergencies can happen anywhere at any time. In Canada\, we fa
 ce numerous hazards\, including wildfires\, flooding\, heatwaves\, and ear
 thquakes. The Be Ready workshop aims to raise individual and household eme
 rgency preparedness.\nDrop-in\; no registration required. For more informa
 tion\, contact the Downsview branch at 416-395-5720 or go to www.tpl.ca/lo
 cations/DO.
LOCATION:Downsview\, Lower Level Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab6913c3dd190003e7487d2
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a2757984407827f8aa38eb3"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Retirement Planning and Living
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261104T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261104T140000
UID:6a2757984407827f8aa38eb3@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:It's never too late to start thinking about investing! Managin
 g your finances to maximize your retirement years is the goal of retiremen
 t planning. Your retirement strategy should strike a balance between your 
 financial realities\, requirements and wants. This presentation will cover
  how to plan for retirement\, sources of retirement income and how to prot
 ect yourself from scams\, frauds and financial abuse.\nPresented by Canadi
 an Investment Regulatory Organization (CIRO)\, a national self-regulatory 
 organization that oversees all investment dealers\, mutual fund dealers an
 d trading activity on Canada’s debt and equity marketplaces.\nhttps://ww
 w.ciro.ca/about-ciro\nDrop-in.
LOCATION:Barbara Frum
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a2757984407827f8aa38eb3
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab29934da318a10e635de12"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Protect Yourself from Financial Scams
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261104T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261104T140000
UID:6ab29934da318a10e635de12@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:A representative from the\nCanada Revenue Agency (CRA)\nwill d
 iscuss how to recognize scams and fraud\, the different methods used by sc
 ammers\, how to protect your personal and financial information\, and what
  steps to take if you believe you have been targeted.\nRegistration encour
 aged\n. Drop-ins are welcome until capacity is reached.\nInformation Colle
 ction Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the T
 oronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20
 (c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program r
 egistration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library han
 dles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@t
 pl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
