SUMMARY:Common Hour: The Eckhardt-Gramatté National Tour with Aemilia Mos
 er
DTSTART:20261105T173000Z
DTEND:20261105T183000Z
DTSTAMP:20260925T184400Z
UID:MEC-0ee7cdb0c30e70bdb04b5c35d009d541@events.yorku.ca
RECURRENCE-ID:20261105T173000Z
SEQUENCE:21
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/
 09/ameliamoser.jpg
CATEGORIES:School of the Arts, Media, Performance &amp\; Design
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260925
DESCRIPTION:York Music is proud to present coloratura soprano Aemilia Mose
 r ( https://www.aemiliamoser.com/ )\, winner of the 49th Eckhardt-Gramatt
 é National Music Competition ( https://www.e-gre.ca/about ) (Voice). The 
 E-Gré Competition is a prestigious national platform celebrating contempo
 rary classical music by Canadian composers.\nThursday\, November 5\, 2026\
 n12:30 – 1:30 p.m. \nTribute Communities Recital Hall\nFREE\nThe Eckhar
 dt-Gramatté National Music Competition for the performance of Canadian an
 d contemporary music\, is a memorial to composer\, pianist\, and violinist
  S.C. (Sonia) Eckhardt-Gramatté\, who spent the last twenty-one years of 
 her life in Manitoba. It fulfills her lifelong dream of creating a means b
 y which the music of contemporary composers could make its presence felt b
 y young musicians on the threshold of their careers. The E-Gré National M
 usic Competition has been held annually since 1976 at Brandon University.\
 nThe Eckhardt-Gramatté Competition acknowledges the support of the Canad
 a Council for the Arts ( https://canadacouncil.ca/ ) to present this natio
 nal tour featuring music by Canadian composers.\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20260925
LOCATION:Tribute Communities Recital Hall\, 112 Accolade East Building\, Y
 ork University
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/the-eckhardt-gramatte-national-tour-nov
 5/
X-SOURCE:York University
END:VEVENT
