SUMMARY:Thursday Night Tech Support Drop-in
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261105T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261105T200000
UID:6a85cd564c610f00389551e2@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Have questions about your tablet\, phone\, laptop\, email or a
 n app? Need help with eBooks or other online library services?\nWe know ke
 eping up with new technology can be difficult! Our staff are here to teach
  you technology tools and concepts in a friendly and casual setting. Pleas
 e bring your personal device and any questions you may have.\n*Longer ques
 tions may be referred to a 1 hour Book a Librarian appointment at a later 
 date.*\n*No technology repairs at this event.*
LOCATION:Guildwood
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a85cd564c610f00389551e2
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a985eb669166f088b96cd93"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Historical Fiction Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261105T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261105T200000
UID:6a985eb669166f088b96cd93@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Are you interested in historical people and events?\nJoin our 
 book club where we will read a wide range of historical fiction titles.\nS
 ept 3:\nThe Night Watchman\nby Louise Erdrich\nPlease reserve your own cop
 y or ask staff for help.\nOct 1:\nWe Do Not Part\nby Han Kang\nPlease rese
 rve your own copy or ask staff for help.\nNov 5:\nMayflies\nby Andrew O'Ha
 gan\nPlease reserve your own copy or ask staff for help.\nDec 3 :\nDaughte
 rs of the Deer\nby Danielle Daniel\nCopies of the book will be available o
 n Nov 5.\nJan 7:\nWhen We Lost Our Heads\nby Heather O'Neill\nPlease reser
 ve your own copy or ask staff for help.
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith\, In the basement program room A
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a985eb669166f088b96cd93
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/696be0372c65973d001863f7"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Beaches Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261105T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261105T200000
UID:696be0372c65973d001863f7@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a lively discussion about the months book pick in 
 a welcoming\, relaxed setting. New members are always welcome and encourag
 ed to join.\nJanuary 8 - The Story of Us by Catherine Hernandez\nFebruary 
 5 - Death of the Author by Nnedi Okarofor\nMarch 5 - Wuthering Heights by 
 Emily Bronte\nApril 2 - The Siren's Call by Chris Hayes\nMay 7 - That Time
  I Loved You by Carianne Leung\nJune 4 - Any Other Way: How Toronto Got Qu
 eer by John Lorinc\nJuly 2 - The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy by Dougl
 as Adams\nAugust 6 - Demon Copperhead by Barbara Kingsolver\nSeptember 3 -
  Noopiming by Leanne Betasamosake Simpson\nOctober 1 - Shadow of the Wind 
 by Carlos Ruiz Zafon\nNovember 5 - House Divided by Alex Bozikovic\nDecemb
 er 3 - The Glass Hotel by Emily St. John Mandel\nCopies of our book club p
 icks will be set aside each month at the first-floor desk at Beaches Libra
 ry. These titles are also available as eBooks and eAudiobooks through Libb
 y\, and in alternate formats.
LOCATION:Beaches\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/696be0372c65973d001863f7
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Teens": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abc169be8cf1c005cafe983"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_teens
SUMMARY:Newcomers Civic Track: 1
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261105T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261105T200000
UID:6abc169be8cf1c005cafe983@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:New to Scarborough? This three-session series is designed for 
 you. Learn how to find local services and community resources online\, bui
 ld a personal map of your neighbourhood\, and create something you can sha
 re with family and friends. Sessions are welcoming\, hands-on\, and delive
 red in plain language. No prior tech experience required\, just bring your
  questions. This is session one in a series\, separate registration requi
 red for each session.\nThis program is part of TPL's Innovator in Residenc
 e series focused on civic innovation. From October 5 to November 28\, join
  programs\, workshops and one-on-one consultations led by technology strat
 egist Ismail Mohamud to learn how technology can help you create positive 
 change in your community. Learn more at\ntpl.ca/iir\n.\nInformation Collec
 tion Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the To
 ronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(
 c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program re
 gistration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library hand
 les your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tp
 l.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Second floor\, Digital Innovation Hub
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abc169be8cf1c005cafe983
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
