SUMMARY:Access to Housing
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261106T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261106T150000
UID:6a79d94fc5fbcf8eb27cc491@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Are you looking for subsidized housing in Toronto?\nThis sessi
 on will cover:\n- An overview of the RGI application process\n- Eligibilit
 y requirements\n- Steps for submitting and updating applications\n- Inform
 ation on priority access\n- The choice-based cycle housing offer process a
 nd the Single Offer Rule\n- Financial assistance programs to help the tena
 nts/home owners\nWhether you are a first-time applicant or seeking assista
 nce with an existing application\, this session will empower you with the 
 knowledge needed to navigate the Rent Geared to Income housing system.\nPr
 esented by The Housing Help Centre (THHC)\, a registered non-profit agency
  whose mandate is to help people access and maintain affordable and safe m
 arket rent accommodation.\nPlease arrive a few minutes early.\nThe persona
 l information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library unde
 r the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The infor
 mation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and
  evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can 
 be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 7
 89 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Learning Centre\, Second Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a79d94fc5fbcf8eb27cc491
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a905cc7be148200298a7306"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:ACT-ively Preventing Elder Abuse 關愛長者：守護長者權益
 工作坊 (English &Chinese)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261106T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261106T160000
UID:6a905cc7be148200298a7306@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Break down the stigma around elder abuse and learn how to reco
 gnize and respond to it in a safe way. Join a facilitator from Theatre of 
 the Beat for this practical and engaging workshop where you'll learn to:\n
 identify the different types of elder abuse\nIdentify the signs of elder a
 buse\nUsing theatre exercises\, develop strategies to be an 'active bystan
 der' in situations where elder abuse might be present. No theatre experien
 ce required\, but participation in role plays is encouraged!\nAbout Theatr
 e of the Beat:\nTheatre of the Beat (TOTB) is a Canadian touring theatre c
 ompany working to catalyze conversations on social justice and its interse
 ction with the beliefs of the communities in which we find ourselves.\nLig
 ht refreshments are provided for all participants. Ingredient lists will b
 e available at the program.\n關愛長者：守護長者權益工作坊\n
 長者是家庭和社區的重要成員。我們都希望長者能夠生
 活得安心、受到尊重，並獲得適切的關懷與支持。\n歡迎
 參加這個互動工作坊，透過討論和戲劇活動，一起認識
 長者在日常生活中可能遇到的困難與挑戰，學習如何關
 心身邊的長者，並在適當的情況下提供支援和協助。\n您
 將有機會學習：\n了解影響長者身心健康及生活福祉的不
 同情況\n認識需要關注的徵兆和訊號\n透過戲劇練習及角
 色扮演，學習如何成為積極的旁觀者，以安全和尊重的
 方式關心及支持有需要的長者\n無需戲劇經驗，歡迎所有
 關心長者福祉的人士參加。活動鼓勵參加者輕鬆投入互
 動練習，在交流中學習實用的關愛技巧。\n關於 Theatre of 
 the Beat\nTheatre of the Beat（TOTB）是一家加拿大巡迴劇團，
 透過戲劇促進社區對社會議題的交流與對話，鼓勵大眾
 共同建立更關愛和包容的社區。\n活動將提供輕便茶點.
LOCATION:Steeles
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a905cc7be148200298a7306
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
