DESCRIPTION:Build on your basic Microsoft Word skills and learn to use Wor
 d more effectively.\nIn this class\, you will:\nPractice new Word skills w
 hile you design a flyer\nFormat text\, margins\, indents\, headers and foo
 ters\nFormat text as columns\nCreate bulleted\, numbered and sorted lists\
 nReview your document with Spelling and Grammar check and Thesaurus\nUpon 
 completion of this class\, you will be able to use even more Word tools to
  design your documents.\nPrerequisites:  Word Basics 1 or equivalent skill
 s. Basic keyboarding and mouse skills required.\nFormat: Hands-on with dem
 onstrations\nRegistration begins October 20th.\nInformation Collection Not
 ice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Pu
 blic Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and
  20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registrati
 on\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your
  information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\,
  416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Brentwood\, Learning Centre\, 2nd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab7cdb265abe8002a7c3908
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
