DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261110T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261110T200000
UID:6aaad677ca248a0029164514@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This session\, the follow up to the November 3rd workshop\, i
 s a hands-on workshop to help you identify\, analyze\, and strategize an a
 ctionable plan on growing your network. This workshop\, with Entrepreneur 
 in Residence (Newcomer Focus)\, Jean Chow\, will determine your networkin
 g quotient as a baseline so that you will be able to measure improvements 
 in your networking skills.\nIn this session:\nKnow your network better by 
 creating your network map.\nKnow how to blend your personal brand with you
 r minimum value proposition created in Week 2.\nIn a group think tank sess
 ion\, you will have Identified a strategy on how to connect with your POI 
 – person of interest – from your relationship circle.\nCome early to n
 etwork from 6-6:30pm!\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal inform
 ation on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Pu
 blic Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information w
 ill only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluat
 ion. Questions about how the library handles your information can be direc
 ted to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge
  Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
