SUMMARY:Blueprint for Change: 3D Design & Printing
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261110T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261110T200000
UID:6abe8972754bb0003ac29745@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In this hands-on session\, you will design and 3D print a phys
 ical response to a civic challenge then explain the thinking behind what y
 ou built. From concept to object\, you will learn the basics of 3D design 
 and discover how making something tangible can sharpen your civic ideas. N
 o design experience required.\nThis program is part of TPL's Innovator in 
 Residence series focused on civic innovation. From October 5 to November 2
 8\, join programs\, workshops and one-on-one consultations led by technolo
 gy strategist Ismail Mohamud to learn how technology can help you create p
 ositive change in your community. Learn more at\ntpl.ca/iir\n.\nInformatio
 n Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected b
 y the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(
 a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and pr
 ogram registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the libr
 ary handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswe
 rline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Second Floor\, Digital Innovation Hub
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abe8972754bb0003ac29745
