BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Toronto Ai Machine Learning Data Science": "https://www.meetup.com/toronto-ai-machine-learning-data-science/events/316489793/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_toronto_ai_machine_learning_data_science
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Toronto AI & ML
UID:event_316489793@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261003T050449Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261111T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261111T203000
SUMMARY:Nov 11 - Toronto Physical AI Workshop and Meetup
DESCRIPTION:Toronto AI\, Machine Learning and Computer Vision Meetup\nJoin
  us at the University of Toronto on November 11 for the Toronto Physical A
 I Workshop and Meetup\, co-presented by Nebius and Voxel51.\n\nSeats are l
 imited\, **[Pre-registration is mandatory.](https://voxel51.com/events/tor
 onto-physical-ai-workshop-and-meetup-november-11-2026)**\n\n**Date\, Time 
 and Location**\n\nNov 11\, 2026\n5:30 PM - 8:30 PM\nThe Conference Centre 
 at U of T\nGiovanni Room (2nd Floor)\n89 Chestnut St.\nToronto\, ON M5G 1R
 1\n\n**Meetup Agenda**\n*5:30–6:30 PM*\n\n* Networking\, food\, drinks\,
  and lightning talks\n\n**Workshop Agenda**\nThis hands-on session uses DR
 OID\, a real-world robotics dataset loaded into FiftyOne as a native multi
 modal MCAP recording\, and YOLO11n\, fine-tuned live during the session.\n
 \n*6:30–7:30 PM*\n\n* Welcome + framing: from raw robot logs to a traine
 d detector\n* Explore a real DROID robotics recording in FiftyOne's native
  multimodal MCAP viewer: camera\, proprioception\, and language on one syn
 ced timeline\, no ROS install required\n* Curate: extract and browse frame
 s from the recording\, filter and deduplicate\n* Compute embeddings on the
  curated frames\; explore via similarity search and embeddings visualizati
 on (via Nebius Serverless AI Jobs)\n\n*7:30–8:00 PM*\n\n* Auto-label: op
 en-vocabulary detection to generate bounding boxes for the robot gripper a
 nd target objects\n* Train: fine-tune a YOLO11n detector on the auto-label
 ed frames (via Nebius Serverless AI Jobs)\n* Evaluate results and close th
 e loop: view predictions back on the original MCAP timeline\n\n*8:00–8:3
 0 PM*\n\n* What else Nebius offers: Token Factory walkthrough — chat/vis
 ion models\, fine-tuning\, credits
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/toronto-ai-machine-learning-data-scie
 nce/events/316489793/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260909T215816Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260909T215816Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Teens": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab2b15eed69cc15475c1139"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_teens
SUMMARY:The Writings of David Thompson on His Travels in North America
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261111T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261111T183000
UID:6ab2b15eed69cc15475c1139@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This presentation examines the historical Writings of David Th
 ompson. Between 1784 and 1812\, David Thompson (1770-1857) explored and tr
 aded over a vast expanse of western North America. Later in life\, the sur
 veyor and fur trader wrote what he called his\nTravels\n\, a spectacular g
 eographical and spirited intellectual journey of the Canadian experience. 
 His story tells of a remarkable life in the fur trade but it also captures
  hid reflections on the land and the indigenous peoples of western North A
 merica.\nPresented by Bill Moreau\, editor of the three-volume work\,\nThe
  Writings of David Thompson\n.\nRegistration is encouraged but not necessa
 ry.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form
  is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act
 \, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used f
 or event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions abo
 ut how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline 
 staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto 
 ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 1\, 2nd floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab2b15eed69cc15475c1139
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
