BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab6d0afda318a10e636c484"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Marketing on a Community Budget
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261111T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261111T200000
UID:6ab6d0afda318a10e636c484@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This program is part of the York Woods Library’s\nEntreprene
 ur in Residenc\ne (EIR) service\nIn this interactive workshop\, participan
 ts define their brand story and state their value in plain language\, shar
 pening it through a message-crafting exercise. The session focuses on mark
 eting that costs little but works well\, such as word of mouth\, community
  partnerships\, and local events. It also shows how to turn first customer
 s into repeat customers and a steady source of referrals.\nDrop-In\nTo app
 ly for one-on-one consultations with our resident entrepreneur\, Leo\, ple
 ase fill out the in-take form available at\ntpl.ca/eir\n. We begin accepti
 ng in-take forms on September 28\, 2026 until available slots are filled.
LOCATION:York Woods\, Enhanced Learning Centre
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab6d0afda318a10e636c484
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69de5e272866a5b4884877f2"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Short Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261111T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261111T193000
UID:69de5e272866a5b4884877f2@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Are you interested in joining a book club but are short on tim
 e?  Then join our Short Book Club\, where we read titles that are 250 page
 s or less. Meetings are held on the second Wednesday of each month.\nOur N
 ovember book is\nObasan\nby Joy Kogawa\nSummary: Based on the author's ow
 n experiences\, this award-winning novel was the first to tell the story o
 f the evacuation\, relocation\, and dispersal of Canadian citizens of Japa
 nese ancestry during the Second World War.\nNew members are most welcome! 
 Please inquire at the circulation desk if you would like a copy of the boo
 k.
LOCATION:Parliament Street\, Main Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69de5e272866a5b4884877f2
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Young Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8f69d42dac6e003721f7f9"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_young_adults
SUMMARY:High Park Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261111T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261111T200000
UID:6a8f69d42dac6e003721f7f9@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Come and join us on the second Wednesday of every month to dis
 cuss a variety of books.\nEveryone is welcome! Drop-in\, no registration r
 equired.\n2026 Reading List:\nJanuary 14:\nWhat I Mean to Say\n: Remaking 
 Conversation in Our Time by Ian Williams\nFebruary 11:\nFahrenheit 451\nby
  Ray Bradbury\nMarch 11:\nThe Remains of the Day\nby Kazuo Ishiguro\nApril
  8:\nOrbital\nby Samantha Harvey\nMay 13:\nThe Empusium\n: A Health Resort
  Horror Story by Olga Tokarczuk\nJune 10:\nTruth Telling\nSeven Conversati
 ons About Indigenous Life in Canada by Michelle Good\nJuly 8:\nThree Days 
 in June\nby Anne Tyler\nAugust 12:\nThe Woman in the Library\nby Sulari Ge
 ntill\nSeptember 9:\nValentine in Montreal\nby Heather O'Neill\nOctober 14
 :\nOn Tyranny: Twenty Lessons from the Twentieth Century\nby Timothy Snyde
 r\nNovember 11:\nFive Tuesdays in Winter\nby Lily King\nDecember 9: Best B
 ooks of the Year Discussion
LOCATION:High Park\, Community Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8f69d42dac6e003721f7f9
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
