SUMMARY:Aki no Tabi | 秋の旅
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261114T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261114T190000
UID:1e43949a1b1cd702dee939d13411dc35@jccc.on.ca
DESCRIPTION:Aki no Tabi — Autumn at the JCCC This fall\, join us at the 
 JCCC for a new seasonal experience celebrating Japanese and Japanese Canad
 ian culture through creativity\, connection\, and hands-on activities. Exp
 lore a variety of workshops and activities\, including: Workshops - Ticket
 s on sale Oct 2\, 2026 at 10am Wagashi Making - Enjoy Daifuku with Atelier
  Wa Ceramics - Autumn Leaves Mamezara with Secret Teatime Crochet - Make Y
 our Own Amigurumi with So Craftful Journaling & Paper Craft - Crafting Our
  Narratives with Erica H. Isomura and Nico Koyanagi Craft activities Live 
 music Food and drink vendors Local market vendors Inspired by the nostalgi
 c charm of Japan and the cozy feeling of autumn transitioning into winter\
 , Aki no Tabi is a place to slow down\, create\, connect\, and enjoy the s
 eason together. Come experience the warmth and nostalgia of autumn at the 
 JCCC. 🍂 Keep an eye on this space for more detailed information in the 
 coming weeks!\n\nCategories: Community Event\, Social
LOCATION:Japanese Canadian Cultural Centre
URL:https://jccc.on.ca/event/2026/11/aki-no-tabi
