SUMMARY:Entrepreneurship Mentorship Makes a Difference for All
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261116T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261116T200000
UID:6aaad6a2ab7a8e0037c241ef@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Whether you are starting a business or in job search\, mentors
 hip is important for newcomers in Canada. Entrepreneur in Residence (Newco
 mer Focus)\, Jean Chow\, shares how a good mentor can bridge gaps and exp
 lain expectations\, real and/or perceived\, and can help newcomers build v
 ital professional networks\, learn and build workplace culture\, and gain 
 confidence.\nIn this session:\nThe Art of Mentorship – what is mentorshi
 p?\nDiscover mentorship programs in the GTA for entrepreneurs.\nStrategies
  on finding a great mentor/mentee.\nCome early to network from 6-6:30pm!\n
 Information Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is c
 ollected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, se
 ctions 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for ev
 ent and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about ho
 w the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff
  at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4
 W 2G8.
LOCATION:Fort York\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aaad6a2ab7a8e0037c241ef
