SUMMARY:NatureTO: Our Urban Forest
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261117T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261117T151500
UID:6a7d07404027d701ebc3fc50@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Toronto has one of the largest urban forests in the world. Joi
 n the City of Toronto Urban Forestry staff for an in-library presentation 
 on this amazing natural habitat that reaches all corners of Toronto. We’
 ll discuss what makes the urban forest so special and share tools to help 
 you explore and understand it better. Bring questions and curiosities\, an
 d leave with greater confidence and a deeper understanding of your City an
 d the natural world around you!\nNo registration. Drop-in\nPresented as pa
 rt of TPL's environmental program series\, Our Fragile Planet.
LOCATION:Locke\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a7d07404027d701ebc3fc50
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
