BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Teens": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abc216511bbf300684a75fc"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_teens
SUMMARY:Newcomers Civic Track: 3
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261117T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261117T200000
UID:6abc216511bbf300684a75fc@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:New to Scarborough? This three-session series is designed for 
 you. Learn how to find local services and community resources online\, bui
 ld a personal map of your neighbourhood\, and create something you can sha
 re with family and friends. Sessions are welcoming\, hands-on\, and delive
 red in plain language. No prior tech experience required\, just bring your
  questions. This is session three in a series\, separate registration req
 uired for each session.\nThis program is part of TPL's Innovator in Reside
 nce series focused on civic innovation. From October 5 to November 28\, jo
 in programs\, workshops and one-on-one consultations led by technology str
 ategist Ismail Mohamud to learn how technology can help you create positiv
 e change in your community. Learn more at\ntpl.ca/iir\n.\nInformation Coll
 ection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the 
 Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 2
 0(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program 
 registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library ha
 ndles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@
 tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Second floor\, Digital Innovation Hub
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abc216511bbf300684a75fc
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
