UID:6a86fda7feae96003806ff65@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:For those of us who may see ourselves as a "work in progress\,
 " come learn and grow together with a selection of classic and popular per
 sonal development titles.\nBooks are first-come\, first-served.\nTo get a 
 copy of the month's book selection\, please ask at the Adult Information D
 esk or call 416-396-3975 to see if a copy is still available. Many titles 
 are also available in other formats for you to place your own hold.\nThe 
 title for the March 19th meeting is:\nCollective Illusions\nThe title for 
 the April 16th meeting is:\nLessons for Living\nThe title for the May 21st
  meeting is:\nThe Let Them Theory\nThe title for the June 18th meeting is:
 \nThe Next Conversation\nThe title for the July 16 meeting is:\nYou're Not
  Listening\nThe title for the August 20th meeting is:\nBig Feelings\nThe t
 itle for the September 17th meeting is:\nLighter\nThe title for the Octobe
 r 15th meeting is:\nThe Power of Now\nThe title for the November 19th meet
 ing is:\nSet Boundaries\, Find Peace\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe 
 personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Libra
 ry under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). Th
 e information will only be used for event and program registration\, deliv
 ery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your informati
 on can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5
 981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:S. Walter Stewart\, Meeting Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a86fda7feae96003806ff65
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
