SUMMARY:Learning Things You Love with AI
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261119T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261119T180000
UID:6a9c345929a7dd0d67493d38@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Always wanted to learn to cook\, draw\, knit\, fix a bike\, or
  speak another language\, but have trouble sticking to it? What if you had
  a personal AI tutor?\nIn this class\, learn how AI can become your person
 al tutor for something you love\, or something new you want to fall in lov
 e with. A tutor explains things in the way you understand\, asks you quest
 ions\, and helps you choose what to learn next. Learn how to turn your goa
 l into a specific\, doable learning experiment: options not answers\, with
  a practice that survives a bad day. Decide ahead of time how you'll know 
 it's working: revise\, or stop without guilt. You'll leave with a plan you
  actually want to try\, and a sense for what AI should never decide for yo
 u.\nPrerequisites: Mouse\, keyboarding and internet skills. Computers ar
 e provided. No coding experience required.\nRegistration is required and 
 will start October 9\, 2026 at 12:30 PM.\nNote: Your spot will not be guar
 anteed after 5 minutes of the start of the program.\nAfter this time\, rem
 aining seats will be filled on a first come\, first serve basis until capa
 city is reached.\nIf you wish to save your work from this hands-on program
 \, please bring your own USB stick.\nAbout the AI Tools Used in This Progr
 am\nThis program includes activities that use agentic AI tools (listed bel
 ow) on library laptops.\nYou do not need to create your own account for th
 is program.\nParticipants are encouraged to follow the Resident’s guidan
 ce throughout sessions\, which include best practices on using AI.\nWe enc
 ourage you to review the privacy statements of each tool prior to attendin
 g this program:\nClaude Code\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy po
 licy\nClaude Cowork\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nGoo
 gle Antigravity\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nGoogle 
 AI Studio\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nInformation C
 ollection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by t
 he Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\
 , 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and progr
 am registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library
  handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerli
 ne@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd Floor eLearning Lab
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9c345929a7dd0d67493d38
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
