BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a877294aafa6100295e0108"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Why We Misunderstand the Middle East—And Why It Matters
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261119T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261119T200000
UID:6a877294aafa6100295e0108@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join Dr. Hamid Yazdi and explore how media narratives\, famili
 ar assumptions\, and everyday language shape public understanding of the 
 region. This talk invites audiences to question simplified explanations an
 d think more critically about what they hear. With real-world implications
  - from public debate to economic ripple effects - getting the Middle East
  right is more important than it seems.\nDrop in\, no registration require
 d.
LOCATION:Brentwood\, Community Room\, Ground Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a877294aafa6100295e0108
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Teens": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abe89da11bbf300684aa7ff"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_teens
SUMMARY:Innovating Civic History
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261119T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261119T200000
UID:6abe89da11bbf300684aa7ff@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:We dig into a real civic issue from the past\, one that was ei
 ther solved\, stalled\, or never fully addressed and ask: what would we do
  differently today? Using modern tools\, fresh perspectives\, and communit
 y knowledge\, participants analyze what happened and propose new approache
 s. History is the starting point\; innovation is the goal.\nThis program i
 s part of TPL's Innovator in Residence series focused on civic innovation.
  From October 5 to November 28\, join programs\, workshops and one-on-one 
 consultations led by technology strategist Ismail Mohamud to learn how tec
 hnology can help you create positive change in your community. Learn more 
 at\ntpl.ca/iir\n.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal informatio
 n on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public
  Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will 
 only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation.
  Questions about how the library handles your information can be directed 
 to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Str
 eet\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Second Floor\, Digital Innovation Hub
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abe89da11bbf300684aa7ff
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
