DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261123T150000
UID:6ab7ceab65abe8002a7c3917@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Practice your Microsoft Word skills when working with long doc
 uments.\nIn this class\, you will:\nUse Styles to effectively format\, str
 ucture and navigate your document\nCreate a Table of Contents\nUse Page an
 d Section breaks\nInsert Page Numbers and Footnotes\nInsert Web and docume
 nt links\nLearn about Microsoft Word's Accessibility features\nUpon comple
 tion of this class\, you will be able to format long documents\, such as b
 ooks\, reports\, and essays.\nPrerequisites:  Word Basics 1\, 2 & 3\, or e
 quivalent skills. Keyboarding and mouse skills are required.\nFormat: Hand
 s-on with demonstrations\nRegistration begins October 20th.\nInformation C
 ollection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by t
 he Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\
 , 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and progr
 am registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library
  handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerli
 ne@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Brentwood\, Learning Centre\, 2nd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab7ceab65abe8002a7c3917
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
