SUMMARY:Artists in the Library: Crochet
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261125T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261125T200000
UID:6aa06943aafa610029625fd0@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:November      4:\nThis workshop will teach participants some b
 asic crochet techniques      like holding the yarn and hook\, chaining\, s
 lip stitching\, and single      crochet stitch.\nNovember      11:\nThis w
 orkshop will build on the crochet techniques learned in the      last work
 shop\, tackling the half double crochet\, double crochet\, and the      tr
 eble crochet stitches.\nNovember      18:\nThis workshop is a self-led cro
 chet session to make space for      participants to create their patches f
 or the communal tapestry. Workshop      materials will be provided for the
  first 15 participants.\nNovember      25:\nThis workshop is a self-led cr
 ochet session to make space for      participants to finish their patches 
 for the communal tapestry. We’ll also      be sewing completed patches t
 o the communal tapestry as they are      completed.\nRegistration required
 . W\norkshop materials will be provided for the first 15 participants. Fee
 l free to drop-in to sessions if you have the supplies needed. We’ll al
 so reflect on and discuss our connections to crochet\, air\, and our commu
 nities.\nThis event is part of the\nArtists in the Library\nprogram.\nInfo
 rmation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is colle
 cted by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sectio
 ns 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event 
 and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how th
 e library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\
 nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G
 8.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Digital Innovation Lab\, 2nd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa06943aafa610029625fd0
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Young Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9b51b13b6c71003e5de7bf"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_young_adults
SUMMARY:Vibe Coding: Make Your Own Interactive Story with AI
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261125T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261125T200000
UID:6a9b51b13b6c71003e5de7bf@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:What if you could write a story where the reader chooses what 
 happens\, like a branching adventure\, a mystery\, or a game\, and have AI
  build it with you?\nIn this class\, you'll learn "vibe-coding": using an 
 AI coding assistant to build your own interactive story or simple game. Yo
 u'll design the branches\, describe the rules in plain language\, test for
  the tricky edge cases (what if the player picks the weird option?)\, and 
 end up with a single file you can share with anyone. Just a story you want
  to tell. This is the playful sibling of the practical vibe-coding worksho
 p.\nPrerequisites: Mouse\, keyboarding and internet skills. Computers ar
 e provided. No coding experience required.\nRegistration is required and 
 will start October 9\, 2026 at 12:30 PM.\nNote: Your spot will not be guar
 anteed after 5 minutes of the start of the program.\nAfter this time\, rem
 aining seats will be filled on a first come\, first serve basis until capa
 city is reached.\nIf you wish to save your work from this hands-on program
 \, please bring your own USB stick.\nAbout the AI Tools Used in This Progr
 am\nThis program includes activities that use agentic AI tools (listed bel
 ow) on library laptops.\nYou do not need to create your own account for th
 is program.\nParticipants are encouraged to follow the Resident’s guidan
 ce throughout sessions\, which include best practices on using AI.\nWe enc
 ourage you to review the privacy statements of each tool prior to attendin
 g this program:\nClaude Code\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy po
 licy\nGoogle Anti-Gravity\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy polic
 y\nGoogle AI Studio\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nInf
 ormation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is coll
 ected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, secti
 ons 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event
  and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how t
 he library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at
 \nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2
 G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd Floor eLearning Lab
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9b51b13b6c71003e5de7bf
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
