SUMMARY:Recovery College: YU & Balance Week 6 | Managing academic stress a
 nd exam anxiety
DTSTART:20261126T170000Z
DTEND:20261126T180000Z
DTSTAMP:20260918T190900Z
UID:MEC-44646f4cd5c4c7d9c6c3f2f6be4dcb1f@events.yorku.ca
RECURRENCE-ID:20261126T170000Z
SEQUENCE:2
CATEGORIES:Academic Advising &amp\; Student Success,Advising,Bethune Colle
 ge,Calumet College,Colleges,Faculties,Faculty of Education,Faculty of Heal
 th,Faculty of Liberal Arts &amp\; Professional Studies,Faculty of Science,
 Glendon,Health Education &amp\; Promotion,LA&amp\;PS Colleges,LA&amp\;PS F
 ounders College,LA&amp\;PS McLaughlin College,LA&amp\;PS New College,LA&am
 p\;PS Vanier College,Lassonde School of Engineering,Learning Commons,Learn
 ing Skills Services,Markham Campus,Markham Student Accessibility Services,
 School of Continuing Studies,School of the Arts, Media, Performance &amp\;
  Design,Stong College,Student Accessibility Services,Student Counselling, 
 Health &amp\; Well-being,Student Leaders at Markham (SLAM),Student Life,St
 udents,Teaching &amp\; Learning,the Atkinson Centre for Mature and Part-ti
 me Students,Well-being
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260918
DESCRIPTION:This session will be offered in person at York University’s 
 Markham Campus and is open to students from all York University campuses.\
 nSometimes\, a single grade can get inside your head and make you question
  your ability to succeed in your program. The pressure to earn high marks
 \, often called “academic perfectionism”\, is something many post-seco
 ndary students experience.\nIn this week’s session of YU & Balance\, par
 ticipants will explore how stress affects academic performance and learn p
 ractical strategies to manage it as you prepare for exam season. By the e
 nd of the session\, participants will have tools to recognize stress\, res
 pond to it effectively\, and protect your confidence during exams.\nThis s
 ession is part of a 6-week Recovery College series. For each session atten
 ded\, participants will receive $5 on their YU-card. To receive the gift c
 ard\, you must attend the full session (approximately 45–60 minutes). Un
 fortunately\, we’re not able to provide gift cards for partial attendanc
 e. Gift cards will be emailed after the session to the same email address 
 used to register and join the session.\nSpace is limited\, and registratio
 n is offered on a first-come\, first-served basis. If the session is full 
 and you’d like to be added to the waitlist\, please email hstacey@yorku.
 ca ( mailto:hstacey@yorku.ca ). We’ll reach out if a spot becomes availa
 ble. If you’re registered but can no longer attend\, please let us know 
 as soon as you can so we can offer your spot to another student.\nRegister
  for Managing academic stress and exam anxiety ( https://forms.students.yo
 rku.ca/view.php?id=501019 )\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20261001
LOCATION:Markham Campus (MK2050)
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/recovery-college-yu-balance-week-6-mana
 ging-academic-stress-and-exam-anxiety/
X-SOURCE:York University
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
