DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261127T160000
UID:6abc00bbde300e004516ffad@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Elevate your holiday season by transforming ordinary gift-givi
 ng into an extraordinary artistic expression. In this engaging\, hands-on 
 workshop\, participants will learn how to design stunning\, boutique-styl
 e holiday packages and personalize gift toppers using paper-sculpting\, pl
 eating techniques\,and repurposed elements. Attendees will leave with two 
 fully styled holiday packages and the skills to make their presents stand 
 out under any tree.\nParticipants are welcome to bring two 6" x 8" boxes\,
  or two small items of a similar size\, to practice wrapping.\nThis worksh
 op will be led by professional craft designer Gabriela Delworth.\nInformat
 ion Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected
  by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 2
 0(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and 
 program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the li
 brary handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nans
 werline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Pape/Danforth\, 2nd floor\, program room.
