BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a85e0cc4c610f0038955592"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Surviving Dementia Care: The Realities of Family Caregiving
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261201T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261201T200000
UID:6a85e0cc4c610f0038955592@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This program will address the experiences of families who are 
 caring for a loved one who is living with dementia\, including the various
  points of stress\, as well as the various points of joy\, and ways in whi
 ch caregivers learn to survive the experience. Major topics include unders
 tanding the diagnosis\, communicating with the loved one\, choosing an ass
 isted living facility\, and using music and the arts as a means of connect
 ion.\nPresented by D. Grant Campbell\, author of "Surviving Dementia Care:
  The Realities of Caregiving" (University of Toronto Press\, 2026).\nDrop-
 in\, but space is limited.\n*\nSpecial guest for the\nTuesday Cards and Ch
 itchat program.
LOCATION:Guildwood
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a85e0cc4c610f0038955592
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a3e8cc6414ef43d00981be7"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Quilting Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261201T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261201T200000
UID:6a3e8cc6414ef43d00981be7@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The focus of this program is to make quilts for donation\, usi
 ng fabrics that have been donated to the group for this purpose.\nParticip
 ants meet weekly to share ideas and inspiration while working on quilts. T
 here are no sewing machines at the library so any sewing is done by hand. 
 Most participants also work on quilts using their own sewing machine at ho
 me. Quilts are completed both as individual projects and as group collabor
 ations.\nNew members are welcome\, and will have access to the instruction
 s\, fabrics\, needle and thread required to contribute on-site to the curr
 ent group project.\nRegarding dates: The quilters will not meet when schoo
 l is out. E.g. March break and during the summer (July and August) and dur
 ing December break.
LOCATION:Jones
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a3e8cc6414ef43d00981be7
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
