BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abc17ba377296003a487737"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Housing Help
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261202T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261202T170000
UID:6abc17ba377296003a487737@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Drop in and work one-on-one with staff from The Housing Help C
 entre (THHC) to determine your housing needs\, connect you to other govern
 ment services\, and to match you with landlords across the city. THHC work
 s with both individuals and families in the City of Toronto to find and ma
 intain affordable\, safe housing.\nThe Housing Help Centre can be contacte
 d at 416-285-8070 or at shhc.ca.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Front Entrance
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abc17ba377296003a487737
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab40c578cf597003f95e9e0"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Chess For Life: Seniors Social
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261202T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261202T153000
UID:6ab40c578cf597003f95e9e0@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The\nChess Institute of Canada (CIC)\ninvites you to join our 
 Chess for Life program - a fun and engaging chess program designed for sen
 iors of all skill levels.\nWhether you’re a seasoned player or intereste
 d in learning the game - enjoy friendly matches\, sharpen your strategy\, 
 and connect with others in a relaxed\, supportive environment. Come make y
 our move!\nFree program. Register for a reminder. Drop-ins are welcome.\n
 Information Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is c
 ollected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, se
 ctions 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for ev
 ent and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about ho
 w the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff
  at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4
 W 2G8.
LOCATION:Ethennonnhawahstihnen'\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab40c578cf597003f95e9e0
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
