SUMMARY:Writers Collective of Canada (WCC): Community Writing Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261207T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261207T200000
UID:6abfc99029c3d600332d2c3d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Experience the transformative power of writing in an inclusive
  space!\nA\nWriters Collective of Canada (WCC)\nworkshop is unlike any oth
 er. We write together\, share first drafts in an encouraging environment\,
  listen deeply to one another\, and receive supportive feedback. Tap into 
 your story and explore your voice in an environment of dignity\, courage\,
  and respect.\nNo experience required. Beginners are welcome. Materials ar
 e provided. Workshops are not sequential\; every workshop is unique - join
  in at any session and let's write together!\nDrop in\, no registration re
 quired\n. Please arrive a few minutes early. For more information\, please
  contact the branch.\n​Presented by Writers Collective of Canada (WCC)\,
  a charitable arts-health organization that ignites connection through cre
 ativity by inspiring powerful\, authentic stories shared in community.\nht
 tps://wcc-cec.org/
LOCATION:Evelyn Gregory
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abfc99029c3d600332d2c3d
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Young Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9b51c2aafa61002961b2a9"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_young_adults
SUMMARY:Vibe Coding: Build Your First App with AI
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261207T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261207T200000
UID:6a9b51c2aafa61002961b2a9@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:What if you could build an app just by describing it\, with no
  coding experience needed? That's vibe coding.\nIn this workshop\, you'll 
 use an AI coding assistant to build your own small\, useful webpage\, chec
 klist\, or organizer from scratch. You'll learn the build loop: describe w
 hat you want\, review the plan\, build one feature\, test it\, fix the bug
 s\, and write documentation so you (or anyone) can understand it later.\nP
 rerequisites: Mouse\, keyboarding and internet skills. Computers are pro
 vided. No coding experience required.\nRegistration is required and will 
 start November 9\, 2026 at 12:30 PM.\nNote: Your spot will not be guarante
 ed after 5 minutes of the start of the program.\nAfter this time\, remaini
 ng seats will be filled on a first come\, first serve basis until capacity
  is reached.\nIf you wish to save your work from this hands-on program\, p
 lease bring your own USB stick.\nAbout the AI Tools Used in This Program\n
 This program includes activities that use agentic AI tools (listed below) 
 on library laptops.\nYou do not need to create your own account for this p
 rogram.\nParticipants are encouraged to follow the Resident’s guidance t
 hroughout sessions\, which include best practices on using AI.\nWe encoura
 ge you to review the privacy statements of each tool prior to attending th
 is program:\nClaude Code\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy
 \nGoogle Antigravity\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nGo
 ogle AI Studio\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nInformat
 ion Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected
  by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 2
 0(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and 
 program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the li
 brary handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nans
 werline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd Floor eLearning Lab
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9b51c2aafa61002961b2a9
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
