BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Young Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa062565ecd9e1b553241ca"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_young_adults
SUMMARY:DJ At Any Age: Memories in the Mix
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261210T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261210T200000
UID:6aa062565ecd9e1b553241ca@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Bring out your inner DJ in this intergenerational program for 
 seniors and adults. Learn basic djing skills and connect with others over 
 a shared love of music. Artist and educator Deejay Vee from At Any Age wil
 l teach you how to use a dj controller and software in a fun and relaxed a
 tmosphere. Working individually or in pairs\, you'll create and exchange p
 laylists of songs that represent meaningful moments in your life.\nNo prio
 r experience needed.\nThis 5-week program series takes place every Thursda
 y from November 12th – December 10th.\nWeeks 1 – 4: Learn DJing skills
 .\nWeek 5: Showcase! Perform your new skills for the group and your friend
 s and family. Refreshments will be provided. Ingredient list will be ava
 ilable at the program.\nInformation Collection Notice\n: The personal info
 rmation on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the 
 Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information
  will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evalu
 ation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be dir
 ected to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yon
 ge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8
LOCATION:Maria A. Shchuka\, 1st Floor\, Children's Programming Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa062565ecd9e1b553241ca
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Young Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a6133043edb05633e8fee18"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_young_adults
SUMMARY:Thursday Night Adventurer's Club (Dungeons and Dragons)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261210T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261210T200000
UID:6a6133043edb05633e8fee18@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Come one come all!\nParticipants will get to experience collab
 orative storytelling at its finest.\nIn this limited Campaign\, participan
 ts will be crafting the world\, their characters\, and potentially the dir
 ection of the story.\nThe campaign will begin with a session of worldbuild
 ing\, character creation\, and a democratic vote on themes and setting. Th
 is will be known as our session zero.\nFollowing sessions will see our cha
 racters progress through a 10 month campaign.(September - June) Relationsh
 ips will be built\, challenges conquered\, and enemies defeated!\n*Program
  is intended for a mature audience\, no prior experience required.\n**Regi
 stration begins Monday August 17 at 12:00pm\n***Space is limited. As a res
 ult we request customers only register for one campaign. (Either Thursday 
 nights or Saturday afternoons.)\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe perso
 nal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library un
 der the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The inf
 ormation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery a
 nd evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information ca
 n be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\,
  789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Port Union\, Meeting Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a6133043edb05633e8fee18
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
