SUMMARY:Creative Writing Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261212T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261212T153000
UID:6a5bce947b79214226a97f52@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Open to adult writers of all experience levels. Monthly meetin
 g with writing peers to work on developing your creative skills. Work on a
 nd share your printed writing (Maximum 500 words) (See registration email 
 for more details)\, hear others’ thoughts\, learn some new writing tips\
 , and participate in creative writing exercises and activities.\nRegistrat
 ion required. Drop-ins welcome if space permits.\nInformation Collection N
 otice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto 
 Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, a
 nd 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registra
 tion\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles yo
 ur information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n
 \, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.\nMore dates to be
  announced.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a5bce947b79214226a97f52
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6931f2a276261f28005d7d70"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Finding Recovery Through Exercise Skills and Hope (FRESH): Movies 
 Saturdays
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261212T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261212T163000
UID:6931f2a276261f28005d7d70@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This program helps people stay active\, make friends\, learn n
 ew skills\, and have fun. Meet new folks\, build connections\, and tell us
  about programs and services you would like to see in the neighbourhood!\n
 Come and join the F.R.E.S.H. group for a Saturday screening of popular mov
 ies.\nWe'll be playing the following films\nOctober 3rd –\nThe Hurrican
 e\nOctober 10th –\nThe Talented Mr. Ripley\nOctober 17th –\nA Simple P
 lan\nOctober 24th –\nScent of a Woman\nOctober 31st –\nThe Silence of
  the Lambs\nDrop in\, no registration is required.\nSnacks and refreshment
 s are provided for all participants. Ingredient lists will be available at
  the program.\nThis program is in collaboration with\nGerstein Crisis Cent
 re's F.R.E.S.H. initiative\n.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, First floor\, Activity Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6931f2a276261f28005d7d70
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
