BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a56c066fb418a28009b035b"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Senior's E-Connect
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261222T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261222T173000
UID:6a56c066fb418a28009b035b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Do you have questions about your tablet\, phone\, laptop\, ema
 il or an app?  Need help with eBooks or other online library services? We
  can help!\nJoin us for this intergenerational program that pairs teen vol
 unteers with seniors to answer your tech questions.\nDrop in\, no registra
 tion is required. Participants may be limited to 1/2 hr sessions.\nEvery T
 uesday\, from 4:00-5:30 pm. Please note\, in April\, program will run ever
 y Tuesday.
LOCATION:Mimico Centennial\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a56c066fb418a28009b035b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Teens": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69711d50992fc18a86deb1ad"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_teens
SUMMARY:Youth Hub: Board Game Café
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261222T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261222T180000
UID:69711d50992fc18a86deb1ad@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us in the Youth Hub every Tuesday to play board games wit
 h your friends! Ask us for our list of board games\, and check our monthly
  calendar for Tournaments with prizes! All materials provided.\nThis progr
 am is part of Youth Hub service. Youth Hubs are a welcoming place for teen
 s after school and in the summer\, where helpful staff are always availabl
 e. Free\, nutritious snacks are offered daily. Drop by a branch with a\n
 Youth Hub\nor call the branch to find out more.
LOCATION:Eatonville
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69711d50992fc18a86deb1ad
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a3d8305f0a66233671b0e44"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Community Writing Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261222T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261222T193000
UID:6a3d8305f0a66233671b0e44@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Experience the transformative power of writing in an inclusive
  space!\nA Writers Collective of Canada (WCC) workshop is unlike any other
 . We write together\, share first drafts in an encouraging environment\, l
 isten deeply to one another\, and receive supportive feedback. Tap into yo
 ur story and explore your voice in an environment of dignity\, courage\, a
 nd respect.\nNo experience required. Beginners are welcome. Materials are 
 provided.
LOCATION:Parliament Street\, Main Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a3d8305f0a66233671b0e44
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
