BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events": "https://events.yorku.ca/events/virtual-drop-in-session-master-of-biotechnology-management-mbm-graduate-diploma-in-biotechnology-gdb-3/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events
SUMMARY:Virtual Drop-In Session: Master of Biotechnology Management (MBM) 
 & Graduate Diploma in Biotechnology (GDB)
DTSTART:20261224T153000Z
DTEND:20261224T160000Z
DTSTAMP:20260721T141200Z
UID:MEC-cd6c652e6f498d4363bff3c4b63bd685@events.yorku.ca__20261224
SEQUENCE:4
CATEGORIES:Faculty of Graduate Studies,Graduate Diploma in Biotechnology,G
 raduate Program in Biotechnology Management
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260721
DESCRIPTION:The Master of Biotechnology Management  is a course- and 
 experiential learning-based graduate program designed for students who 
 hold a bachelor of science degree in biology\, biological sciences\, bio
 technology\, life science\, or related discipline\, and have little/no wor
 k experience in biotechnology. It provides practical interdisciplinary tra
 ining in biotechnology and management to enhance student competitiveness
  and employability in the biotechnology sector. Graduates from this prog
 ram are prepared to contribute to the sector in roles that require scient
 ific\, technical\, and management skills and competencies.  \nThe Grad
 uate Diploma in Biotechnology is a graduate certification for students w
 ho hold a bachelor of science degree in biology\, biological sciences\, 
 biotechnology\, life science\, or related discipline\, and have little/no 
 work experience in biotechnology. It provides scientific and technical 
 training in biotechnology to enhance graduate competitiveness and emplo
 yability in the biotechnology sector. Students acquire the skills and c
 ompetencies required to address labour gaps in the biotechnology sector
  and strengthen the Canadian economy. \nDrop by one of our virtual sessio
 ns on Thursdays from 11:30 a.m. to 12:00 p.m. to meet the graduate pr
 ogram director and graduate program administrator who will be able to answ
 er questions about the programs. \nRegister in advance for this meeting:\
 nMeeting Registration – Zoom\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20260930
PRIORITY:5
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://events.yorku.ca/events/virtual-drop-in-session-master-of-biote
 chnology-management-mbm-graduate-diploma-in-biotechnology-gdb-3/
X-SOURCE:York University
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Teens": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab96380ca248a002918d08a"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_teens
SUMMARY:Youth Hub: Board Games
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261224T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261224T190000
UID:6ab96380ca248a002918d08a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Drop-in casual board game social.\nThis program is part of You
 th Hub service. Youth Hubs are a welcoming place for teens after school an
 d in the summer\, where helpful staff are always available. Free\, nutrit
 ious snacks are offered daily. Drop by a branch with a\nYouth Hub\nor cal
 l the branch to find out more.\nIf you identify as a person with a disabil
 ity or as a person who is Deaf\, and require an accessibility accommodatio
 n to participate in this program\, please contact Accessibility Services b
 y email\naccessibleservices@tpl.ca\n\, or voicemail\, 416-393-7099\, to ma
 ke a request. Please contact us at least three weeks in advance.
LOCATION:Flemingdon Park\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab96380ca248a002918d08a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-ID:gcal_3oo6s709gu7d31cg1419cfrbuc
SUMMARY:Members Night
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261224T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261224T220000
DTSTAMP:20261003T050439Z
UID:00004BF7-8D45-41F7-BDFB-DF9255E8BB54__20261224
SEQUENCE:1
CREATED:20260428T200126Z
DESCRIPTION:Members' Nights Are back! Due to the popularity of members' p
 rojects and general lab activity we've taken the time previously used for 
 MOPs and brought back Members' Nights. If you don't remember Members Nigh
 ts\, they're like open houses but just for members. Think the energy and 
 attendance of open houses but without tours\, etc..\n\nSo come by to work
  on a personal project\, to lend a hand with the ongoing lab renovations\
 , or to conspire (plan something) for a project/event/whatever at Hacklab.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260616T231528Z
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
X-APPLE-CREATOR-IDENTITY:com.apple.mobilecal
X-APPLE-CREATOR-TEAM-IDENTITY:0000000000
X-SOURCE:HackLab.TO
END:VEVENT
