SUMMARY:Chess For Life: Seniors Social
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261229T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261229T110000
UID:6ab3e45f129d8e0031f47449@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Put your mind in play!\nJoin the Chess Institute of Canada (CI
 C) for an engaging social chess experience for adults and seniors. Learn t
 he game\, build your skills\, challenge your thinking and discover new str
 ategies while connecting with fellow players. Whether you're making your f
 irst move or planning three moves ahead\, there's a place at the board for
  you!\nRegister for a reminder. Drop-ins are welcome.
LOCATION:Malvern\, 1st Floor Community Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab3e45f129d8e0031f47449
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a429fd1ed35742f00ff2767"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Finding Recovery Through Exercise Skills and Hope (FRESH)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261229T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261229T130000
UID:6a429fd1ed35742f00ff2767@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This\n program helps people stay active\, make friends\, learn
  new skills\, and \nhave fun. It involves peer-led group activities which 
 can include crafts\, games\,\n walking\, yoga\, and more. Meet new folks\
 , build social connections\, and tell us\n about programs and services you
  would like to see in the neighbourhood!\nOn Tuesdays\, join us for crafts
  (11am-1pm) a walk (11:15am-1pm) and chair yoga (11:30am-12:30pm).\nSnacks
  and refreshments are provided for all participants. Ingredient lists will
  be available at the program.\nThis program is in collaboration with\nGer
 stein Crisis Centre's F.R.E.S.H. initiative\n.
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith\, Varies by program
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a429fd1ed35742f00ff2767
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
