BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aaec6b7129d8e0031f38f8a"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Finding Recovery Through Exercise Skills and Hope (FRESH)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261230T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261230T150000
UID:6aaec6b7129d8e0031f38f8a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This\n program helps people stay active\, make friends\, learn
  new skills\, and \nhave fun. It involves peer-led group activities which 
 can include crafts\, games\,\n walking\, yoga\, and more. Meet new folks\
 , build social connections\, and tell us\n about programs and services you
  would like to see in the neighbourhood!\nFor our upcoming sessions\, we w
 ill be screening the following films in Program Room A:\nOctober 7:\nSingi
 n' in the Rain\nOctober 14:\nCoco\nOctober 21:\nThe Social Network\nOctobe
 r 28:\nThe King's Speech\nNovember 4:\nEternal Sunshine of the Spotless Mi
 nd\nNovember 11:\nLady Bird\nNovember 18:\nJuno\nNovember 25:\nThe Breakfa
 st Club\nDecember 2:\nMy Cousin Vinny\nDecember 9:\nSecondhand Lions\nDece
 mber 16:\nBlack Swan\nDecember 23:\nScrooged\nDecember 30:\nThe Pursuit of
  Happyness\nDrop in. No registration required.\nSnacks and refreshments ar
 e provided for all participants. Ingredient lists will be available at th
 e program.\nThis program is in collaboration with\nGerstein Crisis Centre'
 s F.R.E.S.H. initiative\n.
LOCATION:Maria A. Shchuka\, Meeting Room A
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aaec6b7129d8e0031f38f8a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Young Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a906ac836204e08fbb79755"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_young_adults
SUMMARY:Wednesday Knit & Crochet Circle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261230T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261230T150000
UID:6a906ac836204e08fbb79755@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Want to learn how to knit or crochet with a fun group of peopl
 e? Looking for help with your project?\nYou can also share your projects w
 ith others\, teach or learn a technique\, and enjoy great conversation.\nA
 ll levels of expertise are welcome.\nBring your own yarn\, needles\, and c
 rochet hooks.\nDrop-in only.
LOCATION:Fairview\, Room 201
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a906ac836204e08fbb79755
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abc17ba377296003a48773b"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Housing Help
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261230T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261230T170000
UID:6abc17ba377296003a48773b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Drop in and work one-on-one with staff from The Housing Help C
 entre (THHC) to determine your housing needs\, connect you to other govern
 ment services\, and to match you with landlords across the city. THHC work
 s with both individuals and families in the City of Toronto to find and ma
 intain affordable\, safe housing.\nThe Housing Help Centre can be contacte
 d at 416-285-8070 or at shhc.ca.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Front Entrance
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abc17ba377296003a48773b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/697e3bbccbf6405d3565de39"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Woolly Wednesdays
